{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N9TffStoe59MjX77NMPkJk","type":"tool_result","content":"60\t  the abort signal fires, and the entry calls `process.exit` after flushing\n61\t  stdout and stderr, so no child or handle keeps the process alive\n62\t  (cross-cutting rule \"Process lifetime\", spec.md).\n63\t\n64\t### 2.2 Exit codes\n65\t\n66\t| Code | Name        | When                                                  |\n67\t|------|-------------|-------------------------------------------------------|\n68\t| 0    | Clean       | Command succeeded; review had no gating finding and   |\n69\t|      |             | was not partial. Also help, `--version`, empty diff.  |\n70\t| 1    | Findings    | Review succeeded and `--max-severity` was given and   |\n71\t|      |             | some kept finding's effective severity rank is >= the |\n72\t|      |             | threshold rank. Never produced by an error.           |\n73\t| 2    | Usage       | Any `UsageError`: bad flag, unknown flag or command,  |\n74\t|      |             | positional arg where none allowed, invalid flag value |\n75\t|      |             | or combination, missing/invalid project config, role  |\n76\t|      |             | resolution/validation failure, untrusted config,      |\n77\t|      |             | not in a Git repository (explicit `review`), prompt   |\n78\t|      |             | over the byte ceiling, invalid `--mode` / `--lang`.   |\n79\t| 3    | Auth        | An error wrapping the llm area's auth error kind      |\n80\t|      |             | (provider answered 401/403).                          |\n81\t| 4    | Partial     | Any other error (endpoint failure, resource limits,   |\n82\t|      |             | Git failures, run record write failures), and a       |\n83\t|      |             | successful review that was partial (finder result     |\n84\t|      |             | incomplete, or any kept finding's verdict undecided). |\n85\t| 5    | Cancelled   | An error wrapping cancellation (the abort signal).    |\n86\t\n87\tExit code from an error (`exitCode(err)`), evaluated in order:\n88\t\n89\t1. no error -> 0;\n90\t2. error chain contains cancellation -> 5;\n91\t3. error chain contains the llm auth kind -> 3;\n92\t4. error chain contains a `UsageError` -> 2;\n93\t5. otherwise -> 4.\n94\t\n95\tA successful review returns a non-error \"exit with code\" signal (Go\n96\t`gateExit`) for codes 1 and 4; it carries no message and nothing is written\n97\tto stderr for it, in either error format.\n98\t\n99\tReview exit selection after a completed run (`reviewExitError`), in order:\n100\t\n101\t1. finalizing the run record failed -> that error (exit 4 normally); an\n102\t   artifact failure always wins over the severity gate;\n103\t2. `--max-severity` given and `maxSeverityRank >= thresholdRank` -> exit 1;\n104\t3. partial -> exit 4;\n105\t4. otherwise exit 0.\n106\t\n107\tSeverity ranks: INFO 0, LOW 1, MEDIUM 2, HIGH 3, CRITICAL 4. The result's\n108\tmax severity is the highest effective severity rank (finder area defines\n109\t\"effective\": the verifier may recalibrate) over the kept findings\n110\t(`result.findings`, not dropped ones), or -1 when there are none. So\n111\t`--max-severity INFO` gates on any kept finding and no findings never\n112\tgate.\n113\t\n114\t### 2.3 Error categories\n115\t\n116\tStable machine-readable classification `ErrorCategoryFor(code, err)`,\n117\tevaluated in order:\n118\t\n119\t1. code 0 -> `none`;\n120\t2. code 1 -> `findings`;\n121\t3. chain contains cancellation -> `cancelled`;\n122\t4. chain contains llm auth -> `auth`;\n123\t5. chain contains llm endpoint -> `endpoint`;\n124\t6. chain contains llm budget-exhausted, work-deadline, or no-final-call ->\n125\t   `resource_limit`;\n126\t7. chain contains a `UsageError`, or code is 2 -> `usage`;\n127\t8. code 5 -> `cancelled`;\n128\t9. otherwise -> `partial`.\n129\t\n130\tSo exit 4 carries one of `endpoint`, `resource_limit`, `partial`.\n131\t\n132\t### 2.4 Error output (`--error-format`)\n133\t\n134\t- `--error-format` is a global (persistent) string flag, default `text`,\n135\t  accepted on every command. Allowed values: `text`, `json`. Any other\n136\t  value is a usage error `invalid --error-format \"<v>\" (text|json)`, raised\n137\t  before the command runs. The bad-value error itself is printed in text\n138\t  form.\n139\t- Errors always go to stderr.\n140\t- Text form: one line, `roast: <message>\\n`, where `<message>` is passed\n141\t  through the render area's text sanitizer (`textsafe.Text`): control\n142\t  characters are escaped: a message containing `a`, ESC, `[2J.go`\n143\t  prints as the literal text `a\\x1b[2J.go` and no ESC byte reaches the\n144\t  terminal. Errors can\n145\t  carry Git stderr naming repository paths.\n146\t- JSON form: one JSON object plus newline:\n147\t\n148\t  ```json\n149\t  {\"error_category\":\"usage\",\"message\":\"invalid --format \\\"x\\\"\",\"exit_code\":2}\n150\t  ```\n151\t\n152\t  Keys in this order: `error_category` (section 2.3), `message` (raw error\n153\t  message, not sanitized; JSON escaping makes it safe), `exit_code`.\n154\t  No HTML escaping: `<`, `>`, `&` and U+2028/U+2029 are written as is\n155\t  (Go's encoder escapes them). Parity is defined on parsed JSON, not bytes\n156\t  (cross-cutting rule \"JSON encoding\", spec.md), so `JSON.stringify` output\n157\t  is correct.\n158\t- The format used for an error is the value of `--error-format` as parsed\n159\t  when the command failed. If parsing failed and yargs produced a parsed\n160\t  `--error-format`, that value is used; otherwise `text`. An invalid parsed\n161\t  value is itself reported in text form (section above).\n162\t\n163\t### 2.5 Command tree\n164\t\n165\tRoot command `roast`:\n166\t\n167\t- Short: \"Adversarial cross-model code review\". Long: \"A finder proposes\n168\t  potential defects, then an independent verifier adjudicates each claim\n169\t  against the local checkout.\" Help text need not match cobra exactly, but\n170\t  root help must describe the tool.\n171\t- Takes every `review` flag (section 2.6) and no positional arguments.\n172\t  A positional argument, including an unknown subcommand name such as\n173\t  `roast bogus` or `roast config bogus`, is a usage error (exit 2).\n174\t- `--version` / `-v` on the root only: prints `roast version <S>\\n` to\n175\t  stdout and exits 0, where `<S>` is the build string (section 2.10). No\n176\t  config is read and the gate bootstrap does not run.\n177\t- `--help` / `-h` on any command prints help to stdout and exits 0 with no\n178\t  configuration, Git repository, or network needed. Help shows effective\n179\t  defaults for `--deadline` (10m, 25m with `--scope repo`, 0 disables),\n180\t  `--max-tokens-total` (3000000, 0 disables), `--max-turns` (16, 40 with\n181\t  `--scope repo`), `--request-timeout` (10m, 0 disables).\n182\t- Bare `roast` (no subcommand) behaves as `review` except: if the working\n183\t  directory is not inside a Git repository, it writes\n184\t  `roast: not in a Git repository; cd into one to review, or try\n185\t  \\`roast doctor\\` / \\`roast --help\\`\\n` (one line) to stderr, prints root\n186\t  help to stdout, and exits 0. Explicit `roast review` outside a Git\n187\t  repository is an error (section 2.7).\n188\t\n189\tSubcommands registered on the root (behavior in other areas): `review`,\n190\t`runs`, `gate`, `skill`, `doctor`, `ignore`, `trust`, `init`, `login`,\n191\t`logout`. Must not exist: `config`, `eval`, `install`,\n192\t`internal-update-helper`, `replay`, `completion` (dropped), `runs label`,\n193\t`runs sync`, `runs status`. Group commands with no default action (`gate`,\n194\t`skill`) print their help to stdout and exit 0 when given no subcommand,\n195\tand give a usage error (exit 2) for an unknown subcommand. Hidden\n196\tsubcommand `gate settings` is part of the gate area.\n197\t\n198\tShared argument rules for every command (Go `noArgs`, `usageArgs`,\n199\t`flagUsageError`): an unknown flag, a malformed flag value, or a wrong\n200\tpositional argument count is a `UsageError` (exit 2).\n201\t\n202\t### 2.6 `review` flags\n203\t\n204\t`roast review` and bare `roast` take the same flags. \"Changed\" means the\n205\tflag appeared on the command line, even with a value equal to its\n206\tdefault. Values parsed per section 2.11.\n207\t\n208\t| Flag | Type | Default | Meaning |\n209\t|------|------|---------|---------|\n210\t| `--config` | string | `\"\"` | project config path; empty -> discover |\n211\t| `--base` | string | `\"\"` | diff base ref (default: scope area) |\n212\t| `--uncommitted-only` | bool | false | only uncommitted changes |\n213\t| `--staged` | bool | false | exactly the staged set |\n214\t| `--task` | string | `(not provided)` | what the builder was asked to do |\n215\t| `--format` | string | `both` | `json`, `markdown`, `both` |\n216\t| `--max-severity` | string | `\"\"` | exit 1 threshold, case-insensitive |\n217\t| `--paths` | string slice | none | limit review to these Git pathspecs |\n218\t| `--exclude` | string slice | none | exclude these pathspecs |\n219\t| `--include-vendored` | bool | false | review vendored/generated files |\n220\t| `--mode` | string | `auto` | `code`, `prose`, `mixed`, `auto` |\n221\t| `--quick` | bool | false | single-shot finder, no verification |\n222\t| `--no-verify` | bool | false | skip verification |\n223\t| `--interactive` | bool | false | finder may navigate the checkout |\n224\t| `--max-turns` | int | 16 | max interactive finder turns |\n225\t| `--deadline` | duration | 0 (unset) | finder work deadline |\n226\t| `--request-timeout` | duration | 0 (unset) | per inference request |\n227\t| `--max-tokens-total` | int | 0 (unset) | shared token ceiling |\n228\t| `--max-verified` | int | 25 | max findings sent to verifier |\n229\t| `--max-attempts` | int | 4 | provider/structured-output attempts |\n230\t| `--show-dropped` | bool | false | render malformed/refuted candidates |\n231\t| `--lang` | string slice | none | prompt packs; `none` disables |\n232\t| `--scope` | string | `diff` | `diff` or `repo` (survey triage) |\n233\t| `--author-model` | string | `\"\"` | author model or family |\n234\t| `--finder-base-url` | string | `\"\"` | finder endpoint override |\n235\t| `--finder-model` | string | `\"\"` | finder model override |\n236\t| `--finder-protocol` | string | `\"\"` | `chat`, `responses`, `anthropic` |\n237\t| `--finder-max-output-tokens` | int | 0 | finder output ceiling |\n238\t| `--verifier-base-url` | string | `\"\"` | verifier endpoint override |\n239\t| `--verifier-model` | string | `\"\"` | verifier model override |\n240\t| `--verifier-protocol` | string | `\"\"` | verifier protocol override |\n241\t| `--verifier-max-output-tokens` | int | 0 | verifier output ceiling |\n242\t\n243\tPlus global `--error-format`. Flags take values only through the command\n244\tline; no environment variable sets any of them (removed variables such as\n245\t`ROAST_FINDER_MODEL`, `ROAST_DEADLINE`, `ROAST_AUTHOR_MODEL`,\n246\t`ROAST_NO_HOOK`, `ROAST_SNAPSHOT`, `OPENAI_BASE_URL`, `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`\n247\thave no effect).\n248\t\n249\t### 2.7 Flag validation (before any config is read)\n250\t\n251\tIn this order, each a `UsageError` with the given message:\n252\t\n253\t1. `--staged` and `--uncommitted-only` both set ->\n254\t   `--staged and --uncommitted-only cannot be combined`.\n255\t2. `--format` not in json/markdown/both -> `invalid --format \"<v>\"`.\n256\t3. `--max-turns < 1` -> `max-turns must be positive`.\n257\t4. `--deadline < 0` -> `deadline cannot be negative`.\n258\t5. `--request-timeout < 0` -> `request-timeout cannot be negative`.\n259\t6. `--max-tokens-total < 0` -> `max-tokens-total cannot be negative`.\n260\t7. `--max-verified < 0` -> `max-verified cannot be negative`.\n261\t8. `--max-attempts < 1` -> `max-attempts must be positive`.\n262\t9. `--scope` not diff/repo -> `invalid --scope \"<v>\" (diff|repo)`.\n263\t10. survey (`--scope repo`) with `--quick` ->\n264\t    `--quick cannot run a repository survey; drop --quick`.\n265\t11. survey with `--staged`, `--uncommitted-only`, or non-empty `--base` ->\n266\t    `--scope repo cannot be combined with --staged, --uncommitted-only, or\n267\t    --base`.\n268\t12. `--max-severity` non-empty and not (after upper-casing and trimming)\n269\t    one of INFO, LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH, CRITICAL ->\n270\t    `invalid --max-severity \"<v>\"`. Valid -> threshold rank; absent ->\n271\t    no gate (rank -1).\n272\t\n273\tThese validate the raw flag values, so `--max-attempts=0` is a usage error\n274\teven when the config sets `limits.max_attempts`. `--mode` and `--lang` are\n275\tvalidated later (section 2.8 step 10), after the empty-diff exit. An empty\n276\tdiff therefore exits 0 even with an invalid `--mode` or `--lang`; this is\n277\tkept for Go parity.\n278\t\n279\t### 2.8 Review orchestration\n280\t\n281\tThe gate bootstrap (section 2.9) runs first, before flag validation, for\n282\tbare `roast` and `review` only. Then, in order:\n283\t\n284\t1. **Flag validation** (section 2.7).\n285\t2. **Project config.** `loadProjectConfig(--config)`: path is `--config`\n286\t   as given (relative to cwd) when non-empty; otherwise config area `Find`\n287\t   from cwd upward, stopping at the Git toplevel of cwd, or at cwd itself\n288\t   when cwd is not in a repository. No file found -> `UsageError`\n289\t   `no project config (.roast.json) found between here and the Git\n290\t   toplevel; run \\`npx roast init\\` to create one`. Find or load failure\n291\t   -> `UsageError` with the config area's message. The loaded config gets\n292\t   the stored credentials store for the repository containing cwd\n293\t   (project scope) and the user (credentials area), read lazily.\n294\t3. **Roles.** `ResolveRole(\"finder\")`, `ResolveRole(\"verifier\")`; then\n295\t   apply role flags to each (`applyRoleFlags`): if `--<role>-base-url` or\n296\t   `--<role>-protocol` changed, call config's `OverrideEndpoint(role,\n297\t   resolved, baseURL|undefined, protocol|undefined)` (passing only the\n298\t   changed ones); then if `--<role>-model` changed set the model; if\n299\t   `--<role>-max-output-tokens` changed set it. Then the finder flip:\n300\t   `ResolveFinderFlip(finderRole, --author-model)`; if it returns a note,\n301\t   log it; if it returns a warning, log it; the finder role becomes the\n302\t   flip's role. Then `ValidateRole(\"finder\", ...)`, and\n303\t   `ValidateRole(\"verifier\", ...)` only when verification will run\n304\t   (`doVerify = !quick && !noVerify`). Every failure in this step is a\n305\t   `UsageError` carrying the config area's message (for example\n306\t   `--finder-max-output-tokens=0` fails validation).\n307\t4. **Git root.** `GitRoot(cwd)`; failure -> `UsageError`\n308\t   `not inside a git repository`. (So `review --config <path>` outside a\n309\t   repository fails here with exit 2.)\n310\t5. **Trust.** trust area `requireTrust(repo, cfg, stdin, stderr)`; its\n311\t   error is returned as-is (usage error when untrusted). Nothing is sent\n312\t   anywhere before this passes.\n313\t6. **Scope inputs.** `excludes = cfg.review.excludes ++ --exclude`.\n314\t   Defaults depend on `--quick`: max diff bytes 1_000_000 (quick 200_000),\n315\t   max file context bytes 400_000 (quick 100_000). `maxDiff =\n316\t   limits.max_diff_bytes ?? default`. Build options: base, uncommitted\n317\t   only, staged only, paths, excludes, include vendored, scope kind,\n318\t   `maxFileDiffBytes = maxDiff`.\n319\t7. **Staged pin.** With `--staged`: context area `PinIndexTree(repo)`\n320\t   gives the tree used for all reads; failure -> error\n321\t   `pin staged tree: <inner>` (exit 4). Its OID is passed to scope build\n322\t   as the staged tree OID.\n323\t8. **Build scope.** scope area `Build(repo, opts)`; error returned as-is.\n324\t   Each scope note is logged.\n325\t9. **Empty scope.** If the scope is empty (survey: no files; otherwise the\n326\t   diff is blank after trimming whitespace), write a report (section\n327\t   2.12) with assessment `NO_DIFF`, empty findings, dropped, notes, files\n328\t   reviewed, mode `code`, and the task; create no run record, no\n329\t   snapshot, send no request; exit 0 regardless of `--max-severity`.\n330\t10. **Corpus pinning and snapshot.**\n331\t    - `runID = records.NewRunID()`.\n332\t    - Reviewed input: the diff, or for a survey the manifest\n333\t      (`inputKind` is `diff` or `manifest`).\n334\t    - Unless the scope is staged: snapshot area `PinWorktree(repo)`;\n335\t      success -> reads use the pinned worktree tree; failure -> log\n336\t      `could not pin the working tree (<err>); reading it live with .git,\n337\t      ignored, and denylisted paths blocked` and read live.\n338\t    - `captureSnapshot` (section 2.13). If a snapshot was captured, it is\n339\t      deleted on any exit before the run record is initialized (step 15).\n340\t11. **Grounding, fit, mode, langs.**\n341\t    - Quote grounder over (repo, tree, diff) -- context area.\n342\t    - `originalDiffBytes` = UTF-8 byte length of the diff before fitting.\n343\t    - `maxFileContext = limits.max_file_ctx_bytes ?? default`.\n344\t    - scope area `Fit(scope, maxDiff)` truncates the diff in place and\n345\t      returns the size breakdown; non-empty breakdown means truncated.\n346\t    - Mode: `--mode auto` -> finder area `ClassifyMode(files)`; then the\n347\t      mode must be code/prose/mixed else `UsageError`\n348\t      `invalid --mode \"<flag value>\"`.\n349\t    - Langs (`resolveLangs`): prose -> `[]`; no `--lang` -> finder area\n350\t      `ClassifyLangs(files)`; any value `none` -> must be the only value\n351\t      (else `UsageError` `--lang none cannot be combined with another\n352\t      language pack`), result `[]`; each value must be one of `go`,\n353\t      `react`, `frontend`, `web` (else `UsageError`\n354\t      `unknown language pack \"<v>\"`); result is the flag values in order.\n355\t12. **Prompts.** Finder override path: `prompts.finder_prose` when mode is\n356\t    prose, else `prompts.finder_code`, resolved via `cfg.PromptPath`.\n357\t    System prompt: prompts area `Finder(mode, scopeKind, quick, langs,\n358\t    overridePath)`. Verifier system: `Verifier(cfg.PromptPath(\n359\t    prompts.verifier))`. Errors returned as-is (exit 4). Finder user\n360\t    prompt: survey -> `FinderUser({task, survey:true, manifest})`; else\n361\t    `FinderUser({task, diff, fileContext})` with context area\n362\t    `BuildFileContext(repo, files, maxFileContext, tree)`.\n363\t13. **Budgets** (flag -> config -> default, section 2.14):\n364\t    - `maxTokensTotal`: `--max-tokens-total`, `limits.max_total_tokens`,\n365\t      3_000_000. 0 disables.\n366\t    - `maxVerified`: `--max-verified`, `limits.max_verified`, 25.\n367\t      0 disables the cap.\n368\t    - `requestTimeout`: `--request-timeout`, `limits.request_timeout`,\n369\t      10m. 0 disables.\n370\t    - `maxAttempts`: `--max-attempts`, `limits.max_attempts`, 4.\n371\t    - Ledger: llm area ledger with limit `maxTokensTotal`, shared by both\n372\t      roles.\n373\t    - `interactive = --interactive && !quick`; `maxTurns = --max-turns`.\n374\t      Survey forces `interactive = true` and, when `--max-turns` was not\n375\t      changed, `maxTurns = 40`.\n376\t    - Small-diff downgrade (interactive and not survey): `minLines =\n377\t      interactive.min_diff_lines ?? 80`, `minFiles = interactive.min_files\n378\t      ?? 4`; if (count of `\\n` in the fitted diff) < minLines AND (number\n379\t      of scope files) < minFiles, log `diff is small; using a single\n380\t      structured finder call` and set `interactive = false`.\n381\t    - `deadline`: `--deadline`, `limits.deadline`, default 10m (25m for a\n382\t      survey). If > 0, the finder's absolute deadline is now + duration;\n383\t      0 means none. It bounds the finder only.\n384\t    - `budgets` object (shared by reference with the report and the run\n385\t      meta; key order irrelevant): `deadline_duration` and\n386\t      `request_timeout` as Go duration strings (section 2.11),\n387\t      `max_total_tokens`, `verifier_cap` (= maxVerified), `max_turns`,\n388\t      `max_attempts`, `max_prompt_bytes`; after the review,\n389\t      `ledger_committed_tokens` when the ledger limit > 0.\n390\t    - Finder tools: context area `ExplorationTools(repo, tree)` when\n391\t      interactive, else none.\n392\t    - Confidence floor: `review.quick_confidence_floor` when quick, else\n393\t      `review.confidence_floor` (config area owns defaults).\n394\t14. **Prompt ceiling.** `promptCeiling = limits.max_prompt_bytes ??\n395\t    8_000_000`. If UTF-8 bytes of finder system + finder user >\n396\t    ceiling: `UsageError` `finder prompt is <n> bytes, over the <c>-byte\n397\t    ceiling; narrow the review scope or adjust limits.max_diff_bytes,\n398\t    limits.max_file_ctx_bytes, or limits.max_prompt_bytes in the project\n399\t    config`. No request is sent and the snapshot is deleted.\n400\t15. **Run record init.** Build meta (records area owns the shape):\n401\t    run ID, UTC timestamp (RFC 3339 with nanoseconds in Go; see records\n402\t    area), repo, argv (the argv given to `run`, without the program\n403\t    name), roast `{version, commit}`, scope meta (kind, base, uncommitted\n404\t    only, staged only, include vendored, paths, excludes, base OID,\n405\t    merge-base OID, head OID, survey, staged, files), derived meta (mode,\n406\t    langs, quick, interactive, max turns, confidence floor, do verify,\n407\t    task, max severity as typed, max diff bytes, max file ctx bytes),\n408\t    roles meta for `finder` and `verifier` (profile, base URL, model,\n409\t    protocol, max output tokens, session header, digest of that role's\n410\t    system prompt), snapshot meta, digests (input kind, digest and byte\n411\t    length of the reviewed input, digests of system and user prompts),\n412\t    budgets, env names only (records `CaptureEnv` over\n413\t    `cfg.CredentialEnvNames()`), caveats from the snapshot. Scope base and\n414\t    head OIDs fall back to the snapshot meta's base/head when the scope\n415\t    has none. Then write meta (required) and the artifacts `input`,\n416\t    `finder_system`, `finder_user`, `verifier_system` (required). Any\n417\t    failure: remove the run directory and return\n418\t    `initialize run record: <e>` or `initialize run artifact <name>: <e>`\n419\t    (exit 4; the snapshot is deleted). After success the snapshot is\n420\t    durable and is kept on every later exit.\n421\t16. **Finder.** Response recorder for the run (records area) appends every\n422\t    raw provider response (role, protocol, model, content type, body).\n423\t    Create the finder client (section 2.15); error returned. Log\n424\t    `finder=<model> profile=<profile> protocol=<protocol>\n425\t    endpoint=<base URL>`. Call finder area `Find(signal, client, {system,\n426\t    user, quick, confidenceFloor, interactive, tools, maxTurns, ground,\n427\t    deadline, survey, capture: records finding spill for runID})`. An\n428\t    error is returned (exit per section 2.2; the run directory stays as\n429\t    initialized, unfinalized).\n430\t17. **Verifier.** `usage = {finder: finderClient.usage()}`. `partial =\n431\t    result.incomplete`. When `doVerify` and the result has at least one\n432\t    finding: create the verifier client (error returned); log\n433\t    `verifying <n> finding(s) with <model> (profile=<p> protocol=<p>)`;\n434\t    `result = Verify(signal, client, result, {systemPrompt:\n435\t    verifierSystem, userPrompt(finding), tools: ExplorationTools(repo,\n436\t    tree) (always), maxTurns: 8, maxVerified, ledger, log})`. The verifier\n437\t    `log` callback writes each message plus newline to stderr verbatim\n438\t    (no `roast: ` prefix, no sanitizing). Then `usage.verifier =\n439\t    verifierClient.usage()`, and `partial` becomes true if any kept\n440\t    finding has an undecided verdict. Verifier user prompt per finding:\n441\t    prompts area `VerifierUser({severity, confidence, file, lines,\n442\t    description, codeQuote, fixedCode, fileSnippet})` where `lines` is\n443\t    `?` for none, `N` for one, `first-last` for more, and `fileSnippet`\n444\t    is context area `NumberedSnippet(repo, file, 60_000, tree)`.\n445\t18. **Survey completion** (survey only): `reviewKind = survey_triage`. If\n446\t    the result is incomplete or its stop reason is `deadline`,\n447\t    `token_budget`, or `budget_exhausted`: `completion = partial`,\n448\t    `stopReason` = the result's stop reason or\n449\t    `incomplete_no_submission` when empty. Otherwise `completion =\n450\t    complete`, `stopReason = converged`, and assessment `NO_FINDINGS`\n451\t    becomes `NO_FINDINGS_IN_SAMPLED_AREAS`.\n452\t19. **Report.** Render area report fields: result, mode, files reviewed,\n453\t    task, run ID, budgets, quick, verified (= doVerify), diff truncated,\n454\t    original diff bytes, size breakdown (path, bytes), usage, prompt packs\n455\t    (langs), review kind, completion, manifest file count (= files\n456\t    length), stop reason. Add `ledger_committed_tokens` to budgets when\n457\t    the ledger limit > 0. Prior notes: records area `SeenBefore(repo,\n458\t    findings, 3)`; for each fingerprint, `seen previously in run <runTS>`\n459\t    plus ` (dropped: <reason>)` when it had a drop reason; omitted when\n460\t    none. Write the report (section 2.12).\n461\t20. **Finalize.** Set meta usage (per role: uncached input, cached input,\n462\t    cache write, output tokens, calls) and budgets. Then, each required:\n463\t    write `result.json` artifact (render JSON), write report Markdown\n464\t    (render Markdown with dropped shown, regardless of `--show-dropped`),\n465\t    rewrite meta, resolve run dir, build the run bundle (records area),\n466\t    append the run index (records `Record(report, repo, argv)`, best\n467\t    effort). Errors: `finalize run result: <e>`, `finalize run report:\n468\t    <e>`, `finalize run metadata: <e>`, `resolve run bundle directory:\n469\t    <e>`, `build local run bundle: <e>`. On success log\n470\t    `run <runID> · report <path>` (U+00B7 middle dot) if the report path\n471\t    resolves.\n472\t21. **Exit** per `reviewExitError` (section 2.2).\n473\t\n474\tCancellation behavior that follows from the above (baseline, not a\n475\tdesign choice): cancellation during the finder returns a cancellation\n476\terror -> exit 5, run directory left initialized. Cancellation during\n477\tverification makes each remaining verdict undecided (verifier area does\n478\tnot propagate the error), so the report and run record are still written\n479\tand the exit is 4. Cancellation before the finder starts surfaces from the\n480\tfirst operation that observes the signal.\n481\t\n482\t### 2.9 Gate bootstrap offer\n483\t\n484\tRuns before the command action for bare `roast` and `review` only, and\n485\tonly when `--error-format` is not `json`. Silent no-op when: cwd is not in\n486\ta Git repository; there is no `.roast.json` at the Git toplevel itself\n487\t(`gateConfigPath(repo)` = config `Find(repo, repo)`); or that config fails\n488\tto load. Otherwise call gate area `Bootstrap({repo, out: stderr, noOffer:\n489\t!cfg.gate.offers(), prompt})` where `gate.offers()` is `gate.offer`\n490\tunset or true, and `prompt` (yes/no via section 2.16) is provided only\n491\twhen stdin and stderr are both terminals. A bootstrap error is logged as\n492\t`roast: pre-commit gate setup skipped: <err>` and never fails the\n493\tcommand. `ROAST_NO_HOOK` has no effect.\n494\t\n495\t### 2.10 Version and build info\n496\t\n497\tBuild values: `version` (package version), `commit` (short 7-char Git\n498\tcommit), `date` (committer date, ISO 8601 strict, `git log -1\n499\t--format=%cI`), all injected at build time. Running from source (no\n500\tinjection) reports `dev`, `unknown`, `unknown`. Build\n501\tstring: if version is `dev` or date is `unknown` -> `<version> (commit\n502\t<commit>)`, else `<version> (<commit>, <date>)`. Run meta records\n503\t`{version, commit}`.\n504\t\n505\t### 2.11 Value syntax\n506\t\n507\t- Booleans: `--quick`, `--quick=true`, `--quick=false`, `--quick false`\n508\t  (also `1`, `0`,\n509\t  `t`, `f`, `TRUE`, `FALSE` as in Go `strconv.ParseBool`). There is no\n510\t  `--no-<flag>` negation; `--no-verify` is its own flag.\n511\t- Integers: decimal only, optional sign. Invalid -> usage error naming the\n512\t  flag. Go's `0x`, `0o` and `_` forms are not accepted (accepted yargs\n513\t  difference, spec.md \"CLI parsing\").\n514\t- Durations (Go `time.ParseDuration`): optional sign, then one or more\n515\t  `<number><unit>` with decimal fractions allowed and units `ns`, `us`,\n516\t  `µs`, `μs`, `ms`, `s`, `m`, `h`; `0` alone is valid; empty or unitless\n517\t  non-zero is invalid. Examples: `90s`, `10m`, `1h30m`, `1.5h`, `-1s`.\n518\t  Invalid -> usage error. Negative parses, then fails validation.\n519\t- Duration formatting (Go `Duration.String`), used for `budgets`:\n520\t  `0s` for zero; under one second uses the largest of `ns`, `µs`, `ms`\n521\t  with fraction (`1.5ms`); otherwise `[<h>h][<m>m]<s>s` where seconds may\n522\t  have a fraction and hours/minutes appear once a larger unit is present:\n523\t  `45s`, `3m0s`, `10m0s`, `25m0s`, `1h30m0s`, `1m30.5s`.\n524\t- String slices (`--paths`, `--exclude`, `--lang`): each occurrence is\n525\t  split on plain commas (no CSV quoting, so `--paths '\"a,b\"'` yields\n526\t  `\"a` and `b\"`), results appended across occurrences:\n527\t  `--paths a,b --paths c` -> `[a, b, c]`.\n528\t- Boolean flags may consume a following `true` or `false` token, so\n529\t  `--quick false` is read as the value `false`. Go treated it as a\n530\t  positional and failed with a usage error; this is an accepted yargs\n531\t  difference.\n532\t- Scalar flags given twice: last wins.\n533\t- `--` ends flags; any positional after it is a usage error.\n534\t\n535\t### 2.12 stdout/stderr discipline\n536\t\n537\t- stdout: the JSON report (one line plus newline) when `--format` is\n538\t  `json` or `both`; help; `--version`; other commands' primary output.\n539\t- stderr: the Markdown report plus newline when `--format` is `markdown`\n540\t  or `both` (rendered with `showDropped = --show-dropped`); every log line;\n541\t  gate offer; trust prompt; errors.\n542\t- Log lines (`logf`) are `roast: <text>\\n` with `<text>` sanitized by\n543\t  `textsafe.Text`.\n544\t- Order within one review on stderr: gate bootstrap output, finder flip\n545\t  note then warning, trust prompt/messages, scope notes, pin-failure\n546\t  note, small-diff note, `finder=...` line, finder/llm output, `verifying\n547\t  ...` line, verifier log lines, Markdown report, `run <id> · report\n548\t  <path>`.\n549\t\n550\t### 2.13 Snapshot capture decision (`captureSnapshot`)\n551\t\n552\tInputs: enabled (`cfg.review.snapshotEnabled()`), repo, runID, scope,\n553\tindex tree OID (staged pin OID or empty), worktree pin.\n554\t\n555\t- Disabled -> meta `{reason: \"disabled by review.snapshot\"}`, caveats\n556\t  `[\"Git snapshot capture was disabled; this run cannot be replayed.\"]`.\n557\t- `head` = scope head OID, else snapshot `HeadOID(repo)`. `base` = scope\n558\t  base OID, else (when scope base ref non-empty) `RevOID(repo, base)`.\n559\t- snapshot area `Capture(repo, {runID, headOID, baseOID, indexTree,\n560\t  worktree: pin})`. Failure -> meta `{reason: <err>, head, base}`, caveats\n561\t  `[\"Git snapshot capture failed: <err>\"]`.\n562\t- Success -> meta: captured true, ref, commit, index tree, worktree tree,\n563\t  head, base (from the capture result), `diffPair`: `head..index` if\n564\t  staged, else `head` if survey, else `head..worktree` if scope base ref\n565\t  empty, else `base..worktree`; `fileModes` = `regular and executable\n566\t  files plus symlinks; empty directories are not represented`;\n567\t  `excludedPaths` from the capture. `baseTree` = `TreeOID(repo, src)`\n568\t  where `src` is head for `head..index`, `head..worktree`, `head`, else\n569\t  base; omitted when `src` empty. Caveat `snapshot excluded <n>\n570\t  denylisted untracked path(s)` when n > 0.\n571\t\n572\t### 2.14 Flag -> config -> default resolution\n573\t\n574\t- `configInt(configured, fallback)`: configured value if set (an explicit\n575\t  0 counts as set), else fallback.\n576\t- `flagOrConfigInt(changed, flagValue, configured, fallback)`: flag value\n577\t  if the flag was changed, else `configInt`.\n578\t- `flagOrConfigDuration` likewise for durations.\n579\t- Settings with flags (flag -> config -> default): deadline,\n580\t  request timeout, max tokens total, max verified, max attempts. Settings\n581\t  with config only (config -> default): max diff bytes, max file ctx\n582\t  bytes, max prompt bytes, interactive thresholds, confidence floors,\n583\t  snapshot. `--max-turns` has no config key; survey changes its default.\n584\t- Each invocation re-resolves; flags never persist.\n585\t\n586\t### 2.15 LLM client configuration\n587\t\n588\t`clientConfig(roleName, role, ledger, capture, maxAttempts,\n589\trequestTimeout)`: role name, base URL with all trailing `/` removed, API\n590\tkey, model, protocol, max output tokens, session header, max attempts,\n591\trequest timeout, shared ledger, response capture callback. Both roles use\n592\tthe same ledger, capture, attempts, and timeout.\n593\t\n594\t### 2.16 Terminal helpers (shared)\n595\t\n596\t- `promptYesDefault(out, reader, question)`: writes `<question> [Y/n] `;\n597\t  reads one line; on EOF with empty input -> false; answer trimmed and\n598\t  lower-cased: `\"\"`, `y`, `yes` -> true; anything else -> false. Read\n599\t  errors other than EOF propagate.\n600\t- `interactiveTerminals(stdin, stderr)`: true only when both are real\n601\t  terminal streams (a non-TTY or non-file stream, such as a test buffer,\n602\t  is never a terminal). Swappable module-level function.\n603\t- `openBrowser(url)`: spawn `open <url>` on darwin, `xdg-open <url>`\n604\t  otherwise, detached, not awaited; returns spawn errors only. Callers\n605\t  always print the URL too. Swappable module-level function.\n606\t- `readSecret(out, stdin, lines, prompt)`: writes prompt; if stdin is a\n607\t  TTY, reads one line in raw mode without echo, then writes a newline and\n608\t  returns it trimmed; otherwise reads one line from the shared line reader\n609\t  `lines` (kept across calls so buffered input survives); EOF with no\n610\t  text -> error; result trimmed.\n611\t- One shared line reader per command invocation must serve every prompt\n612\t  in that command (AGENTS.md login note).\n613\t\n614\t## 3. TypeScript module design\n615\t\n616\t### 3.1 Files\n617\t\n618\t```\n619\tsrc/cli.ts                 entry: shebang, signals, run(), exit"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b283ca8-677a-43f7-a7e2-25611b063cf7","uuid":"12605301-0013-4f6e-a3eb-9b26a80389ab","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:28:13.062Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-20-review-tracer-bullet-chat/.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec/01-cli.md","content":"  the abort signal fires, and the entry calls `process.exit` after flushing\n  stdout and stderr, so no child or handle keeps the process alive\n  (cross-cutting rule \"Process lifetime\", spec.md).\n\n### 2.2 Exit codes\n\n| Code | Name        | When                                                  |\n|------|-------------|-------------------------------------------------------|\n| 0    | Clean       | Command succeeded; review had no gating finding and   |\n|      |             | was not partial. Also help, `--version`, empty diff.  |\n| 1    | Findings    | Review succeeded and `--max-severity` was given and   |\n|      |             | some kept finding's effective severity rank is >= the |\n|      |             | threshold rank. Never produced by an error.           |\n| 2    | Usage       | Any `UsageError`: bad flag, unknown flag or command,  |\n|      |             | positional arg where none allowed, invalid flag value |\n|      |             | or combination, missing/invalid project config, role  |\n|      |             | resolution/validation failure, untrusted config,      |\n|      |             | not in a Git repository (explicit `review`), prompt   |\n|      |             | over the byte ceiling, invalid `--mode` / `--lang`.   |\n| 3    | Auth        | An error wrapping the llm area's auth error kind      |\n|      |             | (provider answered 401/403).                          |\n| 4    | Partial     | Any other error (endpoint failure, resource limits,   |\n|      |             | Git failures, run record write failures), and a       |\n|      |             | successful review that was partial (finder result     |\n|      |             | incomplete, or any kept finding's verdict undecided). |\n| 5    | Cancelled   | An error wrapping cancellation (the abort signal).    |\n\nExit code from an error (`exitCode(err)`), evaluated in order:\n\n1. no error -> 0;\n2. error chain contains cancellation -> 5;\n3. error chain contains the llm auth kind -> 3;\n4. error chain contains a `UsageError` -> 2;\n5. otherwise -> 4.\n\nA successful review returns a non-error \"exit with code\" signal (Go\n`gateExit`) for codes 1 and 4; it carries no message and nothing is written\nto stderr for it, in either error format.\n\nReview exit selection after a completed run (`reviewExitError`), in order:\n\n1. finalizing the run record failed -> that error (exit 4 normally); an\n   artifact failure always wins over the severity gate;\n2. `--max-severity` given and `maxSeverityRank >= thresholdRank` -> exit 1;\n3. partial -> exit 4;\n4. otherwise exit 0.\n\nSeverity ranks: INFO 0, LOW 1, MEDIUM 2, HIGH 3, CRITICAL 4. The result's\nmax severity is the highest effective severity rank (finder area defines\n\"effective\": the verifier may recalibrate) over the kept findings\n(`result.findings`, not dropped ones), or -1 when there are none. So\n`--max-severity INFO` gates on any kept finding and no findings never\ngate.\n\n### 2.3 Error categories\n\nStable machine-readable classification `ErrorCategoryFor(code, err)`,\nevaluated in order:\n\n1. code 0 -> `none`;\n2. code 1 -> `findings`;\n3. chain contains cancellation -> `cancelled`;\n4. chain contains llm auth -> `auth`;\n5. chain contains llm endpoint -> `endpoint`;\n6. chain contains llm budget-exhausted, work-deadline, or no-final-call ->\n   `resource_limit`;\n7. chain contains a `UsageError`, or code is 2 -> `usage`;\n8. code 5 -> `cancelled`;\n9. otherwise -> `partial`.\n\nSo exit 4 carries one of `endpoint`, `resource_limit`, `partial`.\n\n### 2.4 Error output (`--error-format`)\n\n- `--error-format` is a global (persistent) string flag, default `text`,\n  accepted on every command. Allowed values: `text`, `json`. Any other\n  value is a usage error `invalid --error-format \"<v>\" (text|json)`, raised\n  before the command runs. The bad-value error itself is printed in text\n  form.\n- Errors always go to stderr.\n- Text form: one line, `roast: <message>\\n`, where `<message>` is passed\n  through the render area's text sanitizer (`textsafe.Text`): control\n  characters are escaped: a message containing `a`, ESC, `[2J.go`\n  prints as the literal text `a\\x1b[2J.go` and no ESC byte reaches the\n  terminal. Errors can\n  carry Git stderr naming repository paths.\n- JSON form: one JSON object plus newline:\n\n  ```json\n  {\"error_category\":\"usage\",\"message\":\"invalid --format \\\"x\\\"\",\"exit_code\":2}\n  ```\n\n  Keys in this order: `error_category` (section 2.3), `message` (raw error\n  message, not sanitized; JSON escaping makes it safe), `exit_code`.\n  No HTML escaping: `<`, `>`, `&` and U+2028/U+2029 are written as is\n  (Go's encoder escapes them). Parity is defined on parsed JSON, not bytes\n  (cross-cutting rule \"JSON encoding\", spec.md), so `JSON.stringify` output\n  is correct.\n- The format used for an error is the value of `--error-format` as parsed\n  when the command failed. If parsing failed and yargs produced a parsed\n  `--error-format`, that value is used; otherwise `text`. An invalid parsed\n  value is itself reported in text form (section above).\n\n### 2.5 Command tree\n\nRoot command `roast`:\n\n- Short: \"Adversarial cross-model code review\". Long: \"A finder proposes\n  potential defects, then an independent verifier adjudicates each claim\n  against the local checkout.\" Help text need not match cobra exactly, but\n  root help must describe the tool.\n- Takes every `review` flag (section 2.6) and no positional arguments.\n  A positional argument, including an unknown subcommand name such as\n  `roast bogus` or `roast config bogus`, is a usage error (exit 2).\n- `--version` / `-v` on the root only: prints `roast version <S>\\n` to\n  stdout and exits 0, where `<S>` is the build string (section 2.10). No\n  config is read and the gate bootstrap does not run.\n- `--help` / `-h` on any command prints help to stdout and exits 0 with no\n  configuration, Git repository, or network needed. Help shows effective\n  defaults for `--deadline` (10m, 25m with `--scope repo`, 0 disables),\n  `--max-tokens-total` (3000000, 0 disables), `--max-turns` (16, 40 with\n  `--scope repo`), `--request-timeout` (10m, 0 disables).\n- Bare `roast` (no subcommand) behaves as `review` except: if the working\n  directory is not inside a Git repository, it writes\n  `roast: not in a Git repository; cd into one to review, or try\n  \\`roast doctor\\` / \\`roast --help\\`\\n` (one line) to stderr, prints root\n  help to stdout, and exits 0. Explicit `roast review` outside a Git\n  repository is an error (section 2.7).\n\nSubcommands registered on the root (behavior in other areas): `review`,\n`runs`, `gate`, `skill`, `doctor`, `ignore`, `trust`, `init`, `login`,\n`logout`. Must not exist: `config`, `eval`, `install`,\n`internal-update-helper`, `replay`, `completion` (dropped), `runs label`,\n`runs sync`, `runs status`. Group commands with no default action (`gate`,\n`skill`) print their help to stdout and exit 0 when given no subcommand,\nand give a usage error (exit 2) for an unknown subcommand. Hidden\nsubcommand `gate settings` is part of the gate area.\n\nShared argument rules for every command (Go `noArgs`, `usageArgs`,\n`flagUsageError`): an unknown flag, a malformed flag value, or a wrong\npositional argument count is a `UsageError` (exit 2).\n\n### 2.6 `review` flags\n\n`roast review` and bare `roast` take the same flags. \"Changed\" means the\nflag appeared on the command line, even with a value equal to its\ndefault. Values parsed per section 2.11.\n\n| Flag | Type | Default | Meaning |\n|------|------|---------|---------|\n| `--config` | string | `\"\"` | project config path; empty -> discover |\n| `--base` | string | `\"\"` | diff base ref (default: scope area) |\n| `--uncommitted-only` | bool | false | only uncommitted changes |\n| `--staged` | bool | false | exactly the staged set |\n| `--task` | string | `(not provided)` | what the builder was asked to do |\n| `--format` | string | `both` | `json`, `markdown`, `both` |\n| `--max-severity` | string | `\"\"` | exit 1 threshold, case-insensitive |\n| `--paths` | string slice | none | limit review to these Git pathspecs |\n| `--exclude` | string slice | none | exclude these pathspecs |\n| `--include-vendored` | bool | false | review vendored/generated files |\n| `--mode` | string | `auto` | `code`, `prose`, `mixed`, `auto` |\n| `--quick` | bool | false | single-shot finder, no verification |\n| `--no-verify` | bool | false | skip verification |\n| `--interactive` | bool | false | finder may navigate the checkout |\n| `--max-turns` | int | 16 | max interactive finder turns |\n| `--deadline` | duration | 0 (unset) | finder work deadline |\n| `--request-timeout` | duration | 0 (unset) | per inference request |\n| `--max-tokens-total` | int | 0 (unset) | shared token ceiling |\n| `--max-verified` | int | 25 | max findings sent to verifier |\n| `--max-attempts` | int | 4 | provider/structured-output attempts |\n| `--show-dropped` | bool | false | render malformed/refuted candidates |\n| `--lang` | string slice | none | prompt packs; `none` disables |\n| `--scope` | string | `diff` | `diff` or `repo` (survey triage) |\n| `--author-model` | string | `\"\"` | author model or family |\n| `--finder-base-url` | string | `\"\"` | finder endpoint override |\n| `--finder-model` | string | `\"\"` | finder model override |\n| `--finder-protocol` | string | `\"\"` | `chat`, `responses`, `anthropic` |\n| `--finder-max-output-tokens` | int | 0 | finder output ceiling |\n| `--verifier-base-url` | string | `\"\"` | verifier endpoint override |\n| `--verifier-model` | string | `\"\"` | verifier model override |\n| `--verifier-protocol` | string | `\"\"` | verifier protocol override |\n| `--verifier-max-output-tokens` | int | 0 | verifier output ceiling |\n\nPlus global `--error-format`. Flags take values only through the command\nline; no environment variable sets any of them (removed variables such as\n`ROAST_FINDER_MODEL`, `ROAST_DEADLINE`, `ROAST_AUTHOR_MODEL`,\n`ROAST_NO_HOOK`, `ROAST_SNAPSHOT`, `OPENAI_BASE_URL`, `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`\nhave no effect).\n\n### 2.7 Flag validation (before any config is read)\n\nIn this order, each a `UsageError` with the given message:\n\n1. `--staged` and `--uncommitted-only` both set ->\n   `--staged and --uncommitted-only cannot be combined`.\n2. `--format` not in json/markdown/both -> `invalid --format \"<v>\"`.\n3. `--max-turns < 1` -> `max-turns must be positive`.\n4. `--deadline < 0` -> `deadline cannot be negative`.\n5. `--request-timeout < 0` -> `request-timeout cannot be negative`.\n6. `--max-tokens-total < 0` -> `max-tokens-total cannot be negative`.\n7. `--max-verified < 0` -> `max-verified cannot be negative`.\n8. `--max-attempts < 1` -> `max-attempts must be positive`.\n9. `--scope` not diff/repo -> `invalid --scope \"<v>\" (diff|repo)`.\n10. survey (`--scope repo`) with `--quick` ->\n    `--quick cannot run a repository survey; drop --quick`.\n11. survey with `--staged`, `--uncommitted-only`, or non-empty `--base` ->\n    `--scope repo cannot be combined with --staged, --uncommitted-only, or\n    --base`.\n12. `--max-severity` non-empty and not (after upper-casing and trimming)\n    one of INFO, LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH, CRITICAL ->\n    `invalid --max-severity \"<v>\"`. Valid -> threshold rank; absent ->\n    no gate (rank -1).\n\nThese validate the raw flag values, so `--max-attempts=0` is a usage error\neven when the config sets `limits.max_attempts`. `--mode` and `--lang` are\nvalidated later (section 2.8 step 10), after the empty-diff exit. An empty\ndiff therefore exits 0 even with an invalid `--mode` or `--lang`; this is\nkept for Go parity.\n\n### 2.8 Review orchestration\n\nThe gate bootstrap (section 2.9) runs first, before flag validation, for\nbare `roast` and `review` only. Then, in order:\n\n1. **Flag validation** (section 2.7).\n2. **Project config.** `loadProjectConfig(--config)`: path is `--config`\n   as given (relative to cwd) when non-empty; otherwise config area `Find`\n   from cwd upward, stopping at the Git toplevel of cwd, or at cwd itself\n   when cwd is not in a repository. No file found -> `UsageError`\n   `no project config (.roast.json) found between here and the Git\n   toplevel; run \\`npx roast init\\` to create one`. Find or load failure\n   -> `UsageError` with the config area's message. The loaded config gets\n   the stored credentials store for the repository containing cwd\n   (project scope) and the user (credentials area), read lazily.\n3. **Roles.** `ResolveRole(\"finder\")`, `ResolveRole(\"verifier\")`; then\n   apply role flags to each (`applyRoleFlags`): if `--<role>-base-url` or\n   `--<role>-protocol` changed, call config's `OverrideEndpoint(role,\n   resolved, baseURL|undefined, protocol|undefined)` (passing only the\n   changed ones); then if `--<role>-model` changed set the model; if\n   `--<role>-max-output-tokens` changed set it. Then the finder flip:\n   `ResolveFinderFlip(finderRole, --author-model)`; if it returns a note,\n   log it; if it returns a warning, log it; the finder role becomes the\n   flip's role. Then `ValidateRole(\"finder\", ...)`, and\n   `ValidateRole(\"verifier\", ...)` only when verification will run\n   (`doVerify = !quick && !noVerify`). Every failure in this step is a\n   `UsageError` carrying the config area's message (for example\n   `--finder-max-output-tokens=0` fails validation).\n4. **Git root.** `GitRoot(cwd)`; failure -> `UsageError`\n   `not inside a git repository`. (So `review --config <path>` outside a\n   repository fails here with exit 2.)\n5. **Trust.** trust area `requireTrust(repo, cfg, stdin, stderr)`; its\n   error is returned as-is (usage error when untrusted). Nothing is sent\n   anywhere before this passes.\n6. **Scope inputs.** `excludes = cfg.review.excludes ++ --exclude`.\n   Defaults depend on `--quick`: max diff bytes 1_000_000 (quick 200_000),\n   max file context bytes 400_000 (quick 100_000). `maxDiff =\n   limits.max_diff_bytes ?? default`. Build options: base, uncommitted\n   only, staged only, paths, excludes, include vendored, scope kind,\n   `maxFileDiffBytes = maxDiff`.\n7. **Staged pin.** With `--staged`: context area `PinIndexTree(repo)`\n   gives the tree used for all reads; failure -> error\n   `pin staged tree: <inner>` (exit 4). Its OID is passed to scope build\n   as the staged tree OID.\n8. **Build scope.** scope area `Build(repo, opts)`; error returned as-is.\n   Each scope note is logged.\n9. **Empty scope.** If the scope is empty (survey: no files; otherwise the\n   diff is blank after trimming whitespace), write a report (section\n   2.12) with assessment `NO_DIFF`, empty findings, dropped, notes, files\n   reviewed, mode `code`, and the task; create no run record, no\n   snapshot, send no request; exit 0 regardless of `--max-severity`.\n10. **Corpus pinning and snapshot.**\n    - `runID = records.NewRunID()`.\n    - Reviewed input: the diff, or for a survey the manifest\n      (`inputKind` is `diff` or `manifest`).\n    - Unless the scope is staged: snapshot area `PinWorktree(repo)`;\n      success -> reads use the pinned worktree tree; failure -> log\n      `could not pin the working tree (<err>); reading it live with .git,\n      ignored, and denylisted paths blocked` and read live.\n    - `captureSnapshot` (section 2.13). If a snapshot was captured, it is\n      deleted on any exit before the run record is initialized (step 15).\n11. **Grounding, fit, mode, langs.**\n    - Quote grounder over (repo, tree, diff) -- context area.\n    - `originalDiffBytes` = UTF-8 byte length of the diff before fitting.\n    - `maxFileContext = limits.max_file_ctx_bytes ?? default`.\n    - scope area `Fit(scope, maxDiff)` truncates the diff in place and\n      returns the size breakdown; non-empty breakdown means truncated.\n    - Mode: `--mode auto` -> finder area `ClassifyMode(files)`; then the\n      mode must be code/prose/mixed else `UsageError`\n      `invalid --mode \"<flag value>\"`.\n    - Langs (`resolveLangs`): prose -> `[]`; no `--lang` -> finder area\n      `ClassifyLangs(files)`; any value `none` -> must be the only value\n      (else `UsageError` `--lang none cannot be combined with another\n      language pack`), result `[]`; each value must be one of `go`,\n      `react`, `frontend`, `web` (else `UsageError`\n      `unknown language pack \"<v>\"`); result is the flag values in order.\n12. **Prompts.** Finder override path: `prompts.finder_prose` when mode is\n    prose, else `prompts.finder_code`, resolved via `cfg.PromptPath`.\n    System prompt: prompts area `Finder(mode, scopeKind, quick, langs,\n    overridePath)`. Verifier system: `Verifier(cfg.PromptPath(\n    prompts.verifier))`. Errors returned as-is (exit 4). Finder user\n    prompt: survey -> `FinderUser({task, survey:true, manifest})`; else\n    `FinderUser({task, diff, fileContext})` with context area\n    `BuildFileContext(repo, files, maxFileContext, tree)`.\n13. **Budgets** (flag -> config -> default, section 2.14):\n    - `maxTokensTotal`: `--max-tokens-total`, `limits.max_total_tokens`,\n      3_000_000. 0 disables.\n    - `maxVerified`: `--max-verified`, `limits.max_verified`, 25.\n      0 disables the cap.\n    - `requestTimeout`: `--request-timeout`, `limits.request_timeout`,\n      10m. 0 disables.\n    - `maxAttempts`: `--max-attempts`, `limits.max_attempts`, 4.\n    - Ledger: llm area ledger with limit `maxTokensTotal`, shared by both\n      roles.\n    - `interactive = --interactive && !quick`; `maxTurns = --max-turns`.\n      Survey forces `interactive = true` and, when `--max-turns` was not\n      changed, `maxTurns = 40`.\n    - Small-diff downgrade (interactive and not survey): `minLines =\n      interactive.min_diff_lines ?? 80`, `minFiles = interactive.min_files\n      ?? 4`; if (count of `\\n` in the fitted diff) < minLines AND (number\n      of scope files) < minFiles, log `diff is small; using a single\n      structured finder call` and set `interactive = false`.\n    - `deadline`: `--deadline`, `limits.deadline`, default 10m (25m for a\n      survey). If > 0, the finder's absolute deadline is now + duration;\n      0 means none. It bounds the finder only.\n    - `budgets` object (shared by reference with the report and the run\n      meta; key order irrelevant): `deadline_duration` and\n      `request_timeout` as Go duration strings (section 2.11),\n      `max_total_tokens`, `verifier_cap` (= maxVerified), `max_turns`,\n      `max_attempts`, `max_prompt_bytes`; after the review,\n      `ledger_committed_tokens` when the ledger limit > 0.\n    - Finder tools: context area `ExplorationTools(repo, tree)` when\n      interactive, else none.\n    - Confidence floor: `review.quick_confidence_floor` when quick, else\n      `review.confidence_floor` (config area owns defaults).\n14. **Prompt ceiling.** `promptCeiling = limits.max_prompt_bytes ??\n    8_000_000`. If UTF-8 bytes of finder system + finder user >\n    ceiling: `UsageError` `finder prompt is <n> bytes, over the <c>-byte\n    ceiling; narrow the review scope or adjust limits.max_diff_bytes,\n    limits.max_file_ctx_bytes, or limits.max_prompt_bytes in the project\n    config`. No request is sent and the snapshot is deleted.\n15. **Run record init.** Build meta (records area owns the shape):\n    run ID, UTC timestamp (RFC 3339 with nanoseconds in Go; see records\n    area), repo, argv (the argv given to `run`, without the program\n    name), roast `{version, commit}`, scope meta (kind, base, uncommitted\n    only, staged only, include vendored, paths, excludes, base OID,\n    merge-base OID, head OID, survey, staged, files), derived meta (mode,\n    langs, quick, interactive, max turns, confidence floor, do verify,\n    task, max severity as typed, max diff bytes, max file ctx bytes),\n    roles meta for `finder` and `verifier` (profile, base URL, model,\n    protocol, max output tokens, session header, digest of that role's\n    system prompt), snapshot meta, digests (input kind, digest and byte\n    length of the reviewed input, digests of system and user prompts),\n    budgets, env names only (records `CaptureEnv` over\n    `cfg.CredentialEnvNames()`), caveats from the snapshot. Scope base and\n    head OIDs fall back to the snapshot meta's base/head when the scope\n    has none. Then write meta (required) and the artifacts `input`,\n    `finder_system`, `finder_user`, `verifier_system` (required). Any\n    failure: remove the run directory and return\n    `initialize run record: <e>` or `initialize run artifact <name>: <e>`\n    (exit 4; the snapshot is deleted). After success the snapshot is\n    durable and is kept on every later exit.\n16. **Finder.** Response recorder for the run (records area) appends every\n    raw provider response (role, protocol, model, content type, body).\n    Create the finder client (section 2.15); error returned. Log\n    `finder=<model> profile=<profile> protocol=<protocol>\n    endpoint=<base URL>`. Call finder area `Find(signal, client, {system,\n    user, quick, confidenceFloor, interactive, tools, maxTurns, ground,\n    deadline, survey, capture: records finding spill for runID})`. An\n    error is returned (exit per section 2.2; the run directory stays as\n    initialized, unfinalized).\n17. **Verifier.** `usage = {finder: finderClient.usage()}`. `partial =\n    result.incomplete`. When `doVerify` and the result has at least one\n    finding: create the verifier client (error returned); log\n    `verifying <n> finding(s) with <model> (profile=<p> protocol=<p>)`;\n    `result = Verify(signal, client, result, {systemPrompt:\n    verifierSystem, userPrompt(finding), tools: ExplorationTools(repo,\n    tree) (always), maxTurns: 8, maxVerified, ledger, log})`. The verifier\n    `log` callback writes each message plus newline to stderr verbatim\n    (no `roast: ` prefix, no sanitizing). Then `usage.verifier =\n    verifierClient.usage()`, and `partial` becomes true if any kept\n    finding has an undecided verdict. Verifier user prompt per finding:\n    prompts area `VerifierUser({severity, confidence, file, lines,\n    description, codeQuote, fixedCode, fileSnippet})` where `lines` is\n    `?` for none, `N` for one, `first-last` for more, and `fileSnippet`\n    is context area `NumberedSnippet(repo, file, 60_000, tree)`.\n18. **Survey completion** (survey only): `reviewKind = survey_triage`. If\n    the result is incomplete or its stop reason is `deadline`,\n    `token_budget`, or `budget_exhausted`: `completion = partial`,\n    `stopReason` = the result's stop reason or\n    `incomplete_no_submission` when empty. Otherwise `completion =\n    complete`, `stopReason = converged`, and assessment `NO_FINDINGS`\n    becomes `NO_FINDINGS_IN_SAMPLED_AREAS`.\n19. **Report.** Render area report fields: result, mode, files reviewed,\n    task, run ID, budgets, quick, verified (= doVerify), diff truncated,\n    original diff bytes, size breakdown (path, bytes), usage, prompt packs\n    (langs), review kind, completion, manifest file count (= files\n    length), stop reason. Add `ledger_committed_tokens` to budgets when\n    the ledger limit > 0. Prior notes: records area `SeenBefore(repo,\n    findings, 3)`; for each fingerprint, `seen previously in run <runTS>`\n    plus ` (dropped: <reason>)` when it had a drop reason; omitted when\n    none. Write the report (section 2.12).\n20. **Finalize.** Set meta usage (per role: uncached input, cached input,\n    cache write, output tokens, calls) and budgets. Then, each required:\n    write `result.json` artifact (render JSON), write report Markdown\n    (render Markdown with dropped shown, regardless of `--show-dropped`),\n    rewrite meta, resolve run dir, build the run bundle (records area),\n    append the run index (records `Record(report, repo, argv)`, best\n    effort). Errors: `finalize run result: <e>`, `finalize run report:\n    <e>`, `finalize run metadata: <e>`, `resolve run bundle directory:\n    <e>`, `build local run bundle: <e>`. On success log\n    `run <runID> · report <path>` (U+00B7 middle dot) if the report path\n    resolves.\n21. **Exit** per `reviewExitError` (section 2.2).\n\nCancellation behavior that follows from the above (baseline, not a\ndesign choice): cancellation during the finder returns a cancellation\nerror -> exit 5, run directory left initialized. Cancellation during\nverification makes each remaining verdict undecided (verifier area does\nnot propagate the error), so the report and run record are still written\nand the exit is 4. Cancellation before the finder starts surfaces from the\nfirst operation that observes the signal.\n\n### 2.9 Gate bootstrap offer\n\nRuns before the command action for bare `roast` and `review` only, and\nonly when `--error-format` is not `json`. Silent no-op when: cwd is not in\na Git repository; there is no `.roast.json` at the Git toplevel itself\n(`gateConfigPath(repo)` = config `Find(repo, repo)`); or that config fails\nto load. Otherwise call gate area `Bootstrap({repo, out: stderr, noOffer:\n!cfg.gate.offers(), prompt})` where `gate.offers()` is `gate.offer`\nunset or true, and `prompt` (yes/no via section 2.16) is provided only\nwhen stdin and stderr are both terminals. A bootstrap error is logged as\n`roast: pre-commit gate setup skipped: <err>` and never fails the\ncommand. `ROAST_NO_HOOK` has no effect.\n\n### 2.10 Version and build info\n\nBuild values: `version` (package version), `commit` (short 7-char Git\ncommit), `date` (committer date, ISO 8601 strict, `git log -1\n--format=%cI`), all injected at build time. Running from source (no\ninjection) reports `dev`, `unknown`, `unknown`. Build\nstring: if version is `dev` or date is `unknown` -> `<version> (commit\n<commit>)`, else `<version> (<commit>, <date>)`. Run meta records\n`{version, commit}`.\n\n### 2.11 Value syntax\n\n- Booleans: `--quick`, `--quick=true`, `--quick=false`, `--quick false`\n  (also `1`, `0`,\n  `t`, `f`, `TRUE`, `FALSE` as in Go `strconv.ParseBool`). There is no\n  `--no-<flag>` negation; `--no-verify` is its own flag.\n- Integers: decimal only, optional sign. Invalid -> usage error naming the\n  flag. Go's `0x`, `0o` and `_` forms are not accepted (accepted yargs\n  difference, spec.md \"CLI parsing\").\n- Durations (Go `time.ParseDuration`): optional sign, then one or more\n  `<number><unit>` with decimal fractions allowed and units `ns`, `us`,\n  `µs`, `μs`, `ms`, `s`, `m`, `h`; `0` alone is valid; empty or unitless\n  non-zero is invalid. Examples: `90s`, `10m`, `1h30m`, `1.5h`, `-1s`.\n  Invalid -> usage error. Negative parses, then fails validation.\n- Duration formatting (Go `Duration.String`), used for `budgets`:\n  `0s` for zero; under one second uses the largest of `ns`, `µs`, `ms`\n  with fraction (`1.5ms`); otherwise `[<h>h][<m>m]<s>s` where seconds may\n  have a fraction and hours/minutes appear once a larger unit is present:\n  `45s`, `3m0s`, `10m0s`, `25m0s`, `1h30m0s`, `1m30.5s`.\n- String slices (`--paths`, `--exclude`, `--lang`): each occurrence is\n  split on plain commas (no CSV quoting, so `--paths '\"a,b\"'` yields\n  `\"a` and `b\"`), results appended across occurrences:\n  `--paths a,b --paths c` -> `[a, b, c]`.\n- Boolean flags may consume a following `true` or `false` token, so\n  `--quick false` is read as the value `false`. Go treated it as a\n  positional and failed with a usage error; this is an accepted yargs\n  difference.\n- Scalar flags given twice: last wins.\n- `--` ends flags; any positional after it is a usage error.\n\n### 2.12 stdout/stderr discipline\n\n- stdout: the JSON report (one line plus newline) when `--format` is\n  `json` or `both`; help; `--version`; other commands' primary output.\n- stderr: the Markdown report plus newline when `--format` is `markdown`\n  or `both` (rendered with `showDropped = --show-dropped`); every log line;\n  gate offer; trust prompt; errors.\n- Log lines (`logf`) are `roast: <text>\\n` with `<text>` sanitized by\n  `textsafe.Text`.\n- Order within one review on stderr: gate bootstrap output, finder flip\n  note then warning, trust prompt/messages, scope notes, pin-failure\n  note, small-diff note, `finder=...` line, finder/llm output, `verifying\n  ...` line, verifier log lines, Markdown report, `run <id> · report\n  <path>`.\n\n### 2.13 Snapshot capture decision (`captureSnapshot`)\n\nInputs: enabled (`cfg.review.snapshotEnabled()`), repo, runID, scope,\nindex tree OID (staged pin OID or empty), worktree pin.\n\n- Disabled -> meta `{reason: \"disabled by review.snapshot\"}`, caveats\n  `[\"Git snapshot capture was disabled; this run cannot be replayed.\"]`.\n- `head` = scope head OID, else snapshot `HeadOID(repo)`. `base` = scope\n  base OID, else (when scope base ref non-empty) `RevOID(repo, base)`.\n- snapshot area `Capture(repo, {runID, headOID, baseOID, indexTree,\n  worktree: pin})`. Failure -> meta `{reason: <err>, head, base}`, caveats\n  `[\"Git snapshot capture failed: <err>\"]`.\n- Success -> meta: captured true, ref, commit, index tree, worktree tree,\n  head, base (from the capture result), `diffPair`: `head..index` if\n  staged, else `head` if survey, else `head..worktree` if scope base ref\n  empty, else `base..worktree`; `fileModes` = `regular and executable\n  files plus symlinks; empty directories are not represented`;\n  `excludedPaths` from the capture. `baseTree` = `TreeOID(repo, src)`\n  where `src` is head for `head..index`, `head..worktree`, `head`, else\n  base; omitted when `src` empty. Caveat `snapshot excluded <n>\n  denylisted untracked path(s)` when n > 0.\n\n### 2.14 Flag -> config -> default resolution\n\n- `configInt(configured, fallback)`: configured value if set (an explicit\n  0 counts as set), else fallback.\n- `flagOrConfigInt(changed, flagValue, configured, fallback)`: flag value\n  if the flag was changed, else `configInt`.\n- `flagOrConfigDuration` likewise for durations.\n- Settings with flags (flag -> config -> default): deadline,\n  request timeout, max tokens total, max verified, max attempts. Settings\n  with config only (config -> default): max diff bytes, max file ctx\n  bytes, max prompt bytes, interactive thresholds, confidence floors,\n  snapshot. `--max-turns` has no config key; survey changes its default.\n- Each invocation re-resolves; flags never persist.\n\n### 2.15 LLM client configuration\n\n`clientConfig(roleName, role, ledger, capture, maxAttempts,\nrequestTimeout)`: role name, base URL with all trailing `/` removed, API\nkey, model, protocol, max output tokens, session header, max attempts,\nrequest timeout, shared ledger, response capture callback. Both roles use\nthe same ledger, capture, attempts, and timeout.\n\n### 2.16 Terminal helpers (shared)\n\n- `promptYesDefault(out, reader, question)`: writes `<question> [Y/n] `;\n  reads one line; on EOF with empty input -> false; answer trimmed and\n  lower-cased: `\"\"`, `y`, `yes` -> true; anything else -> false. Read\n  errors other than EOF propagate.\n- `interactiveTerminals(stdin, stderr)`: true only when both are real\n  terminal streams (a non-TTY or non-file stream, such as a test buffer,\n  is never a terminal). Swappable module-level function.\n- `openBrowser(url)`: spawn `open <url>` on darwin, `xdg-open <url>`\n  otherwise, detached, not awaited; returns spawn errors only. Callers\n  always print the URL too. Swappable module-level function.\n- `readSecret(out, stdin, lines, prompt)`: writes prompt; if stdin is a\n  TTY, reads one line in raw mode without echo, then writes a newline and\n  returns it trimmed; otherwise reads one line from the shared line reader\n  `lines` (kept across calls so buffered input survives); EOF with no\n  text -> error; result trimmed.\n- One shared line reader per command invocation must serve every prompt\n  in that command (AGENTS.md login note).\n\n## 3. TypeScript module design\n\n### 3.1 Files\n\n```\nsrc/cli.ts                 entry: shebang, signals, run(), exit","numLines":560,"startLine":60,"totalLines":1136}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01N9TffStoe59MjX77NMPkJk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLtHmg7VsCBREZMgZ7wW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016CmV48WHzBcWSwji1S9RvW","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-20-review-tracer-bullet-chat/.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec/01-cli.md","offset":614,"limit":520},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14485,"cache_read_input_tokens":72815,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14485},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b283ca8-677a-43f7-a7e2-25611b063cf7","uuid":"fe75b869-6b97-477c-87b6-5dd769256983","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:28:14.672Z","request_id":"req_011ChLtHmXw3EaQNRvqgBkLY","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016CmV48WHzBcWSwji1S9RvW":{"file_path":"/Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-20-review-tracer-bullet-chat/.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec/01-cli.md","offset":614,"limit":520}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016CmV48WHzBcWSwji1S9RvW","type":"tool_result","content":"614\t## 3. TypeScript module design\n615\t\n616\t### 3.1 Files\n617\t\n618\t```\n619\tsrc/cli.ts                 entry: shebang, signals, run(), exit\n620\tsrc/cli/run.ts             run(argv, io): yargs tree, error output\n621\tsrc/cli/errors.ts          UsageError, ExitSignal, exitCode, category\n622\tsrc/cli/review.ts          runReview orchestration (section 2.8)\n623\tsrc/cli/review-flags.ts    flag definitions, parsing, validation\n624\tsrc/cli/resolve.ts         configInt, flagOrConfigInt/Duration,\n625\t                           resolveLangs, applyRoleFlags\n626\tsrc/cli/snapshot-meta.ts   captureSnapshot (section 2.13)\n627\tsrc/cli/config.ts          projectConfigPath, gateConfigPath,\n628\t                           loadProjectConfig, errNo*Config\n629\tsrc/cli/gate-offer.ts      maybeBootstrapGate\n630\tsrc/cli/terminal.ts        promptYesDefault, interactiveTerminals,\n631\t                           openBrowser, readSecret, LineReader\n632\tsrc/cli/log.ts             logf (textsafe + prefix)\n633\tsrc/duration.ts            parseGoDuration, formatGoDuration\n634\tsrc/buildinfo.ts           version, commit, date, buildString()\n635\ttest/cli/*.ts              tests; test/helpers/ for fixtures\n636\t```\n637\t\n638\tSubcommand modules (`src/cli/runs.ts`, `gate.ts`, ...) belong to their\n639\tareas but register through the same builder API (section 3.3).\n640\t\n641\t### 3.2 Run context and the test seam\n642\t\n643\t```ts\n644\texport interface CliIO {\n645\t    stdin:NodeJS.ReadableStream;\n646\t    stdout:NodeJS.WritableStream;\n647\t    stderr:NodeJS.WritableStream;\n648\t    env:Readonly<Record<string, string|undefined>>;\n649\t    cwd:string;\n650\t    signal?:AbortSignal;\n651\t    fetch?:typeof globalThis.fetch;\n652\t}\n653\t\n654\texport interface RunResult {\n655\t    code:number;\n656\t    error?:Error;\n657\t}\n658\t\n659\texport function run (argv:string[], io:CliIO):Promise<RunResult>\n660\t```\n661\t\n662\t- `run` never calls `process.exit`, never reads `process.argv`,\n663\t  `process.env`, or `process.cwd()`, and never touches the real terminal.\n664\t  It writes the error (section 2.4) to `io.stderr` itself and returns\n665\t  `{code, error}` so tests can assert on both.\n666\t- Cross-area requirement: every area reached from `run` takes `cwd`,\n667\t  `env`, `signal`, and (for network) `fetch` from a context object passed\n668\t  down, instead of process globals. `git` is run with `execFile(...,\n669\t  {cwd, env})`. Records resolve `.roast/runs` from `io.cwd`. Credentials\n670\t  read `HOME` / `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` from `io.env`.\n671\t- `fetch` defaults to `globalThis.fetch`; tests pass a wrapper that\n672\t  rewrites the URL origin to the fake server while recording the\n673\t  original host (equivalent of Go `redirectDefaultTransport`). Login's\n674\t  loopback callback client uses the real `fetch`.\n675\t- `signal` defaults to a never-aborting signal.\n676\t\n677\t```ts\n678\t// src/cli.ts (entry)\n679\tconst controller = new AbortController()\n680\t// onSignal: first signal aborts, second exits 130 (see below)\n681\tprocess.on('SIGINT', onSignal)\n682\tprocess.on('SIGTERM', onSignal)\n683\tconst { code } = await run(process.argv.slice(2), {\n684\t    stdin: process.stdin,\n685\t    stdout: process.stdout,\n686\t    stderr: process.stderr,\n687\t    env: process.env,\n688\t    cwd: process.cwd(),\n689\t    signal: controller.signal,\n690\t})\n691\t// flush both streams, then exit\n692\tprocess.exit(code)\n693\t```\n694\t\n695\tThe entry waits for stdout/stderr writes to flush (write callback or\n696\t`drain`) before `process.exit`, so piped JSON output is never cut off. It\n697\talways calls `process.exit`, even on success, so a lingering child or\n698\thandle cannot hold the process open. An `EPIPE` on stdout is caught by an\n699\t`error` listener on `process.stdout`: it never prints a stack trace and the\n700\tprocess exits quietly with the already computed exit code. A second SIGINT\n701\tor SIGTERM calls `process.exit(130)` directly:\n702\t\n703\t```ts\n704\tlet signalled = false\n705\tconst onSignal = ():void => {\n706\t    if (signalled) process.exit(130)\n707\t    signalled = true\n708\t    controller.abort(new CancelledError())\n709\t}\n710\t```\n711\t\n712\tNode version check: the first statements of `src/cli.ts` compare\n713\t`process.versions.node` with 22.18 (numeric major/minor) and, when lower,\n714\twrite the error and `process.exit(2)` before any other module is imported\n715\t(dynamic `import()` of the CLI body follows the check).\n716\t\n717\tEvery tool that spawns a process (git runner, `openBrowser`, hook helpers)\n718\ttakes `signal` and kills the child (`SIGTERM`, then `SIGKILL` after a short\n719\tgrace) when it aborts.\n720\t\n721\t### 3.3 Errors\n722\t\n723\t```ts\n724\texport const ExitCode = {\n725\t    Clean: 0, Findings: 1, Usage: 2, Auth: 3, Partial: 4, Cancelled: 5,\n726\t} as const\n727\t\n728\texport type ErrorCategory = 'none'|'findings'|'usage'|'auth'|'endpoint'|\n729\t    'resource_limit'|'partial'|'cancelled'\n730\t\n731\texport class UsageError extends Error {}\n732\texport class CancelledError extends Error {}  // name 'AbortError'-aware\n733\t// Successful review asking for a non-zero exit (Go gateExit).\n734\texport class ExitSignal extends Error {\n735\t    constructor (readonly code:1|4) { super(`exit ${code}`) }\n736\t}\n737\t\n738\texport function errorChainHas (\n739\t    err:unknown,\n740\t    test:(e:Error) => boolean\n741\t):boolean   // walks err, err.cause, ... (cycle-safe)\n742\t\n743\texport function isCancellation (err:unknown, signal?:AbortSignal):boolean\n744\texport function exitCode (err:unknown, signal?:AbortSignal):number\n745\texport function errorCategoryFor (code:number, err:unknown):ErrorCategory\n746\texport function writeError (\n747\t    out:NodeJS.WritableStream,\n748\t    code:number,\n749\t    err:Error,\n750\t    format:'text'|'json'\n751\t):void\n752\t```\n753\t\n754\t- Wrapping preserves Go message concatenation: `new Error(\\`pin staged\n755\t  tree: ${inner.message}\\`, {cause: inner})`. Category/exit detection\n756\t  walks `cause`.\n757\t- llm area exports its error kinds (auth, endpoint, budget exhausted,\n758\t  work deadline, no final call) as classes or a tagged `kind` property;\n759\t  `errorCategoryFor` imports them.\n760\t- Cancellation: an error in the chain that is a `CancelledError`, or an\n761\t  `AbortError` raised while `io.signal` is aborted with a\n762\t  `CancelledError` reason. A `TimeoutError` from `AbortSignal.timeout`\n763\t  is never cancellation (Go `DeadlineExceeded` is not `Canceled`).\n764\t\n765\t### 3.4 yargs setup\n766\t\n767\t```ts\n768\tyargs(argv)\n769\t    .scriptName('roast')\n770\t    .locale('en')\n771\t    .detectLocale(false)   // English only, whatever LANG/LC_ALL say\n772\t    .parserConfiguration({\n773\t        'boolean-negation': false,   // --no-verify is a real flag\n774\t        'camel-case-expansion': false,\n775\t        'dot-notation': false,\n776\t        'parse-numbers': false,      // ints parsed by our helper\n777\t        'parse-positional-numbers': false,\n778\t        'duplicate-arguments-array': false, // scalar: last wins\n779\t        'strip-aliased': true,\n780\t    })\n781\t    .strict()\n782\t    .exitProcess(false)\n783\t    .fail((msg, err) => { throw err ?? new UsageError(msg) })\n784\t    .option('error-format', { type: 'string', default: 'text',\n785\t        global: true })\n786\t    .version(false)          // custom root-only --version / -v\n787\t    .help('help').alias('help', 'h')\n788\t    .command(['review', '$0'], ..., reviewBuilder, reviewHandler)\n789\t    .command(runsCommand) // ... other areas\n790\t```\n791\t\n792\t- Output capture: parse with the callback form so yargs returns help and\n793\t  error text instead of printing; `run` writes help to `io.stdout`.\n794\t- Root-only `--version`/`-v`: handled in `run` before command dispatch\n795\t  when it is a root-level flag (no subcommand token precedes it); on a\n796\t  subcommand it is an unknown flag.\n797\t- Bare vs explicit review: the handler checks whether the first\n798\t  positional token was `review`; only bare `roast` gets the\n799\t  not-in-a-Git-repository help path (section 2.5).\n800\t- \"Changed\" detection: review flags with a meaningful \"changed\" state\n801\t  (`max-turns`, `deadline`, `request-timeout`, `max-tokens-total`,\n802\t  `max-verified`, `max-attempts`, all `--<role>-*` flags) are declared\n803\t  without a yargs `default`; `undefined` means not changed and the\n804\t  documented default is applied in `review-flags.ts`. Help text states\n805\t  the defaults in the description.\n806\t- All int and duration flags are declared `type: 'string'` and parsed by\n807\t  `parseIntFlag` / `parseGoDuration`; failures are `UsageError`.\n808\t- Slice flags are declared `type: 'string', array: true` and each element\n809\t  is split on plain commas; a test pins `--paths a,b --paths c`. Booleans\n810\t  keep yargs `type: 'boolean'` with `--flag=false` support; `--quick false`\n811\t  is read as a value (accepted difference from Go) and a test pins it.\n812\t- yargs is pinned to English with `.locale('en')` and `.detectLocale(false)`\n813\t  so messages never depend on the environment.\n814\t- `--error-format` validation and the gate bootstrap run in a yargs\n815\t  middleware (or at the top of each handler) after parsing, before the\n816\t  action, in that order. On a parse failure, `run` uses the parsed\n817\t  `--error-format` if yargs produced it, else `text`.\n818\t- Group commands (`gate`, `skill`) register a handler that prints help\n819\t  when there is no subcommand; `.strict()` makes unknown subcommands\n820\t  usage errors.\n821\t\n822\t### 3.5 Review orchestration types\n823\t\n824\t```ts\n825\texport interface ReviewFlags {\n826\t    config:string; base:string; uncommittedOnly:boolean;\n827\t    staged:boolean; task:string; format:'json'|'markdown'|'both';\n828\t    maxSeverity:string; paths:string[]; exclude:string[];\n829\t    includeVendored:boolean; mode:string; quick:boolean;\n830\t    noVerify:boolean; interactive:boolean; maxTurns?:number;\n831\t    deadlineMs?:number; requestTimeoutMs?:number;\n832\t    maxTokensTotal?:number; maxVerified?:number; maxAttempts?:number;\n833\t    showDropped:boolean; lang:string[]; scope:'diff'|'repo';\n834\t    authorModel:string; finder:RoleFlags; verifier:RoleFlags;\n835\t}\n836\texport interface RoleFlags {\n837\t    baseUrl?:string; model?:string; protocol?:string;\n838\t    maxOutputTokens?:number;\n839\t}\n840\texport function validateReviewFlags (f:ReviewFlags):number // gate rank\n841\texport function runReview (f:ReviewFlags, ctx:RunContext):Promise<void>\n842\texport function resolveLangs (\n843\t    flags:string[], files:string[], mode:string\n844\t):string[]\n845\texport function applyRoleFlags (\n846\t    name:'finder'|'verifier', role:ResolvedRole, flags:RoleFlags\n847\t):ResolvedRole\n848\texport function flagOrConfig<T> (\n849\t    flag:T|undefined, configured:T|undefined, fallback:T\n850\t):T\n851\t```\n852\t\n853\t`runReview` throws `UsageError`, other errors, or `ExitSignal`; it never\n854\twrites the error itself. Durations are carried in milliseconds as\n855\tnumbers internally; `formatGoDuration(ms)` produces budget strings (Go\n856\tnanosecond precision beyond ms is not needed for flags; config durations\n857\tuse the same parser, see config area). Snapshot cleanup uses\n858\t`try/finally` with a `durable` flag, matching the Go `defer`.\n859\t\n860\tDependencies: config, credentials, trust, scope, context, prompts, llm,\n861\tfinder, verifier, render (incl. textsafe), records, snapshot, gate,\n862\tbuildinfo, duration, `@substrate-system/debug` (`roast:cli`).\n863\t\n864\t### 3.6 Build info\n865\t\n866\tVersion, commit, and build date are injected at build time; from source\n867\tthey are `dev` / `unknown` / `unknown`. esbuild `define`s\n868\t`__ROAST_VERSION__` (from `package.json`),\n869\t`__ROAST_COMMIT__` (`git rev-parse --short=7 HEAD`), `__ROAST_DATE__`\n870\t(`git log -1 --format=%cI`), each falling back to `dev` / `unknown` /\n871\t`unknown` when unavailable. `src/buildinfo.ts` exports them and\n872\t`buildString()`. Tests run unbundled code where the globals are absent:\n873\t`buildinfo.ts` reads them through `typeof` guards.\n874\t\n875\t### 3.7 Test fixtures\n876\t\n877\t- `test/helpers/env.ts`: `cleanEnv(base)` returns a copy of an env with\n878\t  every variable whose upper-cased name starts with `ANTHROPIC_`,\n879\t  `OPENAI_`, `OPENROUTER_`, or `ROAST_` removed. Tests build `io.env`\n880\t  from it (plus `PATH`, `HOME` isolation, and explicit variables); no\n881\t  test mutates `process.env`.\n882\t- `test/helpers/inference-stream.ts`: `writeInferenceStream(res,\n883\t  protocol, response)` turns a complete response object into the native\n884\t  SSE stream for `anthropic`, `responses`, or `chat`, exactly as in\n885\t  section 3.8. `writeJSONStream(res, protocol, body)` parses a JSON\n886\t  string first. Unknown protocol -> error.\n887\t- `test/helpers/run.ts`: `runRoast(args, opts)` wraps `run` with buffer\n888\t  streams, a temp repo cwd, clean env, and an optional redirecting\n889\t  `fetch`; returns `{code, error, stdout, stderr}`.\n890\t- Terminal and browser swaps: `simulateTerminals(t, value)` and\n891\t  `captureBrowser(t)` replace the module-level functions and restore\n892\t  them at test end.\n893\t\n894\t### 3.8 SSE fixture format (`writeInferenceStream`)\n895\t\n896\tSets `Content-Type: text/event-stream`. Each event is\n897\t`[event: <name>\\n]data: <json>\\n\\n`. For `responses`, every emitted\n898\tobject gets `sequence_number` 0, 1, 2, ... in emission order.\n899\t\n900\t- `anthropic`: `message_start` with `message` = response with `content:\n901\t  []`, `stop_reason: null`, `usage` copied with `output_tokens: 0`. For\n902\t  each content block at index i: `content_block_start` (`index`,\n903\t  `content_block` = block with `thinking` and `signature` emptied for\n904\t  thinking, `text` emptied for text, `input: {}` for tool use); deltas\n905\t  (`thinking_delta` + `signature_delta`; `text_delta`; or\n906\t  `input_json_delta` with `partial_json` = JSON of the input);\n907\t  `content_block_stop`. Then `message_delta` (`delta: {stop_reason,\n908\t  stop_sequence: null}`, `usage` = response usage) and `message_stop`.\n909\t  Event name = the object's `type`.\n910\t- `responses`: `response.created` (`response` with `output: []`,\n911\t  `status: in_progress`); per output item: `response.output_item.added`\n912\t  (item with `arguments: \"\"`, `status: in_progress`),\n913\t  `response.function_call_arguments.delta` (`item_id`, `delta` =\n914\t  arguments), `response.function_call_arguments.done` (`arguments`),\n915\t  `response.output_item.done` (full item), each with `output_index`;\n916\t  then `response.completed` with the full response.\n917\t- `chat`: no `event:` lines. Three chunks, each `{id, object:\n918\t  \"chat.completion.chunk\", created: 1, model, choices}`: first, choices\n919\t  with `delta` = message with `tool_calls` re-indexed (`index` = position)\n920\t  and `finish_reason: null`; second, choices with empty `delta` and the\n921\t  real `finish_reason`; third, `choices: []` plus `usage`. Then\n922\t  `data: [DONE]\\n\\n`.\n923\t\n924\t## 4. Deliberate changes\n925\t\n926\t1. The cobra `completion` command is dropped.\n927\t2. Windows is not supported: `openBrowser` uses `open` (darwin) or\n928\t   `xdg-open` (linux) only.\n929\t3. Node `>=22.18`, checked at startup; below it the CLI prints a clear\n930\t   error and exits 2 (spec.md change 3).\n931\t4. Debug tracing via `@substrate-system/debug` namespace `roast:cli`\n932\t   (`DEBUG=roast:*`), never including request/response bodies, headers,\n933\t   prompts, or credentials.\n934\t5. First TypeScript release is `2.0.0`; build info comes from esbuild\n935\t   defines instead of Go ldflags / `debug.ReadBuildInfo`.\n936\t6. Help text wording and layout come from yargs and need not match\n937\t   cobra.\n938\t7. A second SIGINT or SIGTERM force-exits with status 130; Go ignored\n939\t   repeats (spec.md change 22). Ctrl-C (`\\x03`) at a raw-mode secret prompt\n940\t   is cancellation, exit 5.\n941\t8. Accepted yargs parsing differences: decimal-only integers, `--quick\n942\t   false` read as a value, plain comma splitting of list flags (spec.md\n943\t   \"CLI parsing\").\n944\t9. JSON error output is not HTML-escaped; parity is on parsed JSON.\n945\t10. EPIPE on stdout exits quietly with the computed code instead of dying\n946\t    by SIGPIPE.\n947\t11. A parse failure reports in the parsed `--error-format` when yargs\n948\t    produced one, else text.\n949\t\n950\tNot a change: the gate bootstrap's terminal check uses the swappable\n951\t`interactiveTerminals(io.stdin, io.stderr)` instead of Go's direct check\n952\tof the process's stdin/stderr; in production these are the same streams.\n953\t\n954\t## 5. Test plan\n955\t\n956\tAll at the `run(argv, io)` seam with a `node:http` fake inference server\n957\tunless noted. Assert exit codes, JSON, files, and requests; never exact\n958\thuman-readable text.\n959\t\n960\tExit codes and errors:\n961\t\n962\t- Exit code constants 0..5 (TestExitCodeContract) -- unit.\n963\t- Category mapping for clean, findings, usage, auth, endpoint, budget,\n964\t  cancelled, partial (TestErrorCategoryFor) -- unit on\n965\t  `errorCategoryFor` with wrapped errors.\n966\t- `review --error-format json --format invalid` in a Git repo -> exit 2,\n967\t  stderr parses as `{error_category: \"usage\", exit_code: 2}` with a\n968\t  message (TestJSONErrorOutput).\n969\t- Text error output escapes control bytes (TestWriteErrorEscapesControls)\n970\t  -- unit on `writeError`.\n971\t- Artifact failure wins over the severity gate\n972\t  (TestReviewExitErrorPrefersArtifactFailureOverFindingGate) -- unit.\n973\t- `--max-attempts=0`, `--request-timeout=-1s`, `--max-tokens-total=-1`,\n974\t  `--finder-max-output-tokens=0` with `--quick --uncommitted-only` -> exit\n975\t  2, category usage (TestInvalidResourceOverridesAreUsageErrors).\n976\t- Unknown subcommands and wrong arg counts -> exit 2: `gate bogus`,\n977\t  `config bogus`, `skill bogus`, `runs show` (0 and 2 args), `runs\n978\t  checkout` (0 and 3 args); `gate` and `skill` alone -> exit 0 with help\n979\t  on stdout (TestCommandUsageErrorsExitWithUsageCode).\n980\t- `runs sync`, `runs status` -> exit 2 (TestRunsUploadSubcommandsAreUnknown).\n981\t- New: SIGINT-equivalent abort during the finder -> exit 5, category\n982\t  `cancelled` (signal passed through `io.signal`).\n983\t- New: `--version` exits 0 and prints the build string on stdout.\n984\t- New: a second abort-style signal force-exits 130 -- entry-level test\n985\t  spawning the built CLI against a fake server that never answers, sending\n986\t  SIGINT twice (first alone gives exit 5); no child process remains.\n987\t- New: `\\x03` fed to the raw-mode secret prompt -> cancellation, exit 5\n988\t  (unit on `readSecret` with a fake TTY stream).\n989\t- New: Node below 22.18 -> exit 2 with an error on stderr (unit on the\n990\t  version-check function with injected version strings).\n991\t- New: EPIPE on a closed stdout pipe -> no stack trace, exit code equals\n992\t  the computed code (entry-level test piping into a closed reader).\n993\t- New: parse failure with `--error-format json` parsed -> JSON error;\n994\t  with none parsed -> text.\n995\t- New: `--paths a,b --paths c` splits to three entries; `--max-attempts\n996\t  0x10` -> exit 2; `--quick false` is read as false; JSON error output\n997\t  compared as parsed JSON (message containing `<>&` round-trips).\n998\t- New: empty diff with invalid `--mode` -> exit 0.\n999\t\n1000\tCommand surface and help:\n1001\t\n1002\t- `--help` exits 0 with no config (TestHelpNeedsNoConfiguration).\n1003\t- Required commands exist and forbidden ones do not, including no\n1004\t  `runs label` (TestPublicCommandSurface) -- assert via running\n1005\t  `<cmd> --help` exit codes rather than introspection.\n1006\t- Review help states effective defaults (TestReviewHelpShowsEffectiveDefaults)\n1007\t  -- keep only as a loose check that the four default numbers appear, or\n1008\t  drop as brittle.\n1009\t- Bare `roast` outside Git -> exit 0, help on stdout\n1010\t  (TestBareCommandOutsideGitShowsHelp).\n1011\t- `review --config <file>` outside Git -> exit 2\n1012\t  (TestExplicitReviewOutsideGitStillFails).\n1013\t- `runs`, `runs prune --dry-run` work in a repo\n1014\t  (TestRunsLocalSubcommandsStillWork).\n1015\t\n1016\tPipeline (end to end with fake server):\n1017\t\n1018\t- Finder + verifier on a custom endpoint, `--format json --max-severity\n1019\t  HIGH` with all budgets 0 and `--max-attempts=1` -> exit 1, confirmed\n1020\t  finding in JSON, run bundle and `provider_responses` captured for both\n1021\t  roles, meta budgets record 0s / 0 / 1, role meta records profile,\n1022\t  protocol, session header; session header sent only by the finder\n1023\t  profile; `runs show`, `runs checkout`, `runs` work on the run; only\n1024\t  inference requests reach the server\n1025\t  (TestFinderVerifierPipelineWithMockEndpoint).\n1026\t- Anthropic-protocol finder with chat verifier\n1027\t  (TestNativeAnthropicFinderWithChatVerifier).\n1028\t- `--scope repo` sends the manifest, uses interactive tools, two finder\n1029\t  requests (TestRepositorySurveyUsesManifestAndInteractiveTools).\n1030\t- Corpus pinned without a snapshot (no HEAD; `review.snapshot: false`):\n1031\t  verifier reads the pinned file, severity canonicalized, exit 1\n1032\t  (TestReviewPinsCorpusWithoutSnapshot).\n1033\t- Run records live under the Git toplevel even with the config in a\n1034\t  subdirectory and cwd deeper (TestRunRecordsLiveUnderProjectToplevel).\n1035\t\n1036\tSettings resolution:\n1037\t\n1038\t- Config limits appear in meta budgets and derived meta\n1039\t  (TestLimitsInProjectConfigBoundTheReview).\n1040\t- `limits.max_diff_bytes` truncates the finder diff\n1041\t  (TestMaxDiffBytesInProjectConfigTruncatesTheDiff).\n1042\t- `limits.max_prompt_bytes` too small -> exit 2, no request\n1043\t  (TestMaxPromptBytesInProjectConfigRejectsALargePrompt).\n1044\t- Invalid limits -> non-zero, no request (TestInvalidLimitsAreRejected).\n1045\t- Interactive thresholds: small diff downgrades `--interactive`; zero\n1046\t  thresholds keep it (TestInteractiveThresholdsInProjectConfig).\n1047\t- `review.snapshot` false -> no snapshot, no `refs/roast/` refs\n1048\t  (TestReviewSnapshotSettingInProjectConfig).\n1049\t- Flags override config for one invocation only, including\n1050\t  `--finder-model` (TestFlagsOverrideProjectConfigForOneInvocation).\n1051\t- Removed environment variables change nothing (defaults in budgets,\n1052\t  no request to env-named endpoints)\n1053\t  (TestRemovedEnvironmentVariablesHaveNoEffect).\n1054\t- `--author-model` flips the finder; `ROAST_AUTHOR_MODEL` does not\n1055\t  (TestAuthorModelFlagSelectsTheFinderFlip,\n1056\t  TestAuthorModelEnvironmentDoesNotFlipTheFinder).\n1057\t- Role flag credential rules (TestProtocolFlagMovesAnUnmodifiedDefaultEndpoint,\n1058\t  TestProtocolFlagClearsWrongProviderCredential,\n1059\t  TestBaseURLFlagDoesNotCarryAmbientProviderKey) -- config area unit\n1060\t  tests of `OverrideEndpoint`, plus one CLI test that a changed\n1061\t  `--finder-base-url` withholds the ambient key.\n1062\t- Gate offer: `gate.offer: false` suppresses it without using it up;\n1063\t  `ROAST_NO_HOOK` does not suppress it; invalid gate settings -> exit 2\n1064\t  (TestGateOfferFalseStopsTheGateOffer,\n1065\t  TestNoHookEnvironmentDoesNotStopTheGateOffer,\n1066\t  TestInvalidGateSettingsAreRejected). Assert the offer through gate\n1067\t  state or a stable marker, not prose.\n1068\t\n1069\tConfig discovery (CLI level; config area owns details):\n1070\t\n1071\t- JSONC config used; nearest config below the toplevel; `--config`\n1072\t  overrides discovery; invalid config rejected; missing config is a usage\n1073\t  error naming `npx roast init`; user config directory not read;\n1074\t  `config init --from-url` unknown (TestReviewUsesModelsFromJSONCProjectConfig,\n1075\t  TestReviewUsesNearestProjectConfigBelowGitToplevel,\n1076\t  TestConfigFlagOverridesDiscoveredProjectConfig,\n1077\t  TestReviewRejectsInvalidProjectConfig,\n1078\t  TestReviewWithoutProjectConfigNamesRoastInit,\n1079\t  TestUserConfigDirectoryIsNotRead, TestConfigInitFromURLIsUnknown).\n1080\t- Prompt override paths resolve against the config directory\n1081\t  (TestPromptOverrideResolvesAgainstConfigDirectory,\n1082\t  TestPromptOverrideFromSubdirectoryWithoutLocalCopy).\n1083\t\n1084\tTerminal and trust prompt (trust area owns, seam shared):\n1085\t\n1086\t- Inline trust prompt approves on yes, declined sends nothing,\n1087\t  non-terminal fails closed (TestInlineTrustPromptApprovesOnYes,\n1088\t  TestInlineTrustPromptDeclinedSendsNothing,\n1089\t  TestNonTerminalReviewFailsClosedWithoutPrompting).\n1090\t- Default terminal detection rejects non-file streams\n1091\t  (TestDefaultTerminalDetectionRejectsNonFiles) -- unit.\n1092\t\n1093\tLower seams (unit): `parseGoDuration` / `formatGoDuration` round trips\n1094\t(`0s`, `45s`, `3m0s`, `1h30m0s`, `1.5ms`), `resolveLangs`,\n1095\t`flagOrConfig`, `captureSnapshot` diff pair selection, `cleanEnv`\n1096\t(TestClearAmbientEnvironmentUnsetsProviderVariables), `buildString`\n1097\tformats (replaces TestResolve, which tested Go toolchain metadata and is\n1098\tnot ported), `promptYesDefault` answers including EOF.\n1099\t\n1100\t## 6. Go baseline references\n1101\t\n1102\tAt commit `cd08f10`:\n1103\t\n1104\t- `cmd/roast/main.go`\n1105\t- `internal/cli/cli.go`, `internal/cli/config.go`,\n1106\t  `internal/cli/prompt.go`\n1107\t- `internal/buildinfo/buildinfo.go`, `scripts/build.ts` (ldflags)\n1108\t- `internal/testutil/env.go`, `internal/testutil/inference.go`\n1109\t- Tests: `internal/cli/cli_test.go`, `settings_test.go`,\n1110\t  `project_config_test.go`, `records_test.go`, `hardening_test.go`,\n1111\t  `prompt_override_test.go`, `trust_prompt_test.go`, `main_test.go`,\n1112\t  `internal/buildinfo/buildinfo_test.go`,\n1113\t  `internal/testutil/env_test.go`\n1114\t- Behavior read from neighbors: `internal/review/types.go` (severity\n1115\t  ranks, `MaxSeverity`), `internal/verify/verify.go` (verifier errors\n1116\t  become undecided verdicts), `internal/llm/provider.go` (context error\n1117\t  normalization), `internal/scope/scope.go` (`GitRoot`, `Empty`),\n1118\t  `internal/config/config.go` (`Gate.Offers`).\n1119\t\n1120\t## 7. Resolved\n1121\t\n1122\t1. JSON error output: parity is on parsed JSON, no HTML escaping\n1123\t   (spec.md, \"JSON encoding\").\n1124\t2. Parse failure uses the parsed `--error-format` when yargs produced one,\n1125\t   else text (spec.md, \"CLI parsing\").\n1126\t3. Integer flags are decimal only, an accepted yargs difference (spec.md,\n1127\t   \"CLI parsing\").\n1128\t4. `--quick false` is read as a value by yargs: accepted (spec.md, \"CLI\n1129\t   parsing\").\n1130\t5. List flags split on plain commas: accepted (spec.md, \"CLI parsing\").\n1131\t6. A second Ctrl-C force-exits 130; Ctrl-C at a raw-mode secret prompt is\n1132\t   cancellation, exit 5 (spec.md, change 22).\n1133\t7. EPIPE on stdout exits quietly with the computed exit code (spec.md,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b283ca8-677a-43f7-a7e2-25611b063cf7","uuid":"0eb4e9d2-231c-4a3e-ad58-c2c643fd4466","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:28:14.710Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-20-review-tracer-bullet-chat/.scratch/ts-rewrite/spec/01-cli.md","content":"## 3. TypeScript module design\n\n### 3.1 Files\n\n```\nsrc/cli.ts                 entry: shebang, signals, run(), exit\nsrc/cli/run.ts             run(argv, io): yargs tree, error output\nsrc/cli/errors.ts          UsageError, ExitSignal, exitCode, category\nsrc/cli/review.ts          runReview orchestration (section 2.8)\nsrc/cli/review-flags.ts    flag definitions, parsing, validation\nsrc/cli/resolve.ts         configInt, flagOrConfigInt/Duration,\n                           resolveLangs, applyRoleFlags\nsrc/cli/snapshot-meta.ts   captureSnapshot (section 2.13)\nsrc/cli/config.ts          projectConfigPath, gateConfigPath,\n                           loadProjectConfig, errNo*Config\nsrc/cli/gate-offer.ts      maybeBootstrapGate\nsrc/cli/terminal.ts        promptYesDefault, interactiveTerminals,\n                           openBrowser, readSecret, LineReader\nsrc/cli/log.ts             logf (textsafe + prefix)\nsrc/duration.ts            parseGoDuration, formatGoDuration\nsrc/buildinfo.ts           version, commit, date, buildString()\ntest/cli/*.ts              tests; test/helpers/ for fixtures\n```\n\nSubcommand modules (`src/cli/runs.ts`, `gate.ts`, ...) belong to their\nareas but register through the same builder API (section 3.3).\n\n### 3.2 Run context and the test seam\n\n```ts\nexport interface CliIO {\n    stdin:NodeJS.ReadableStream;\n    stdout:NodeJS.WritableStream;\n    stderr:NodeJS.WritableStream;\n    env:Readonly<Record<string, string|undefined>>;\n    cwd:string;\n    signal?:AbortSignal;\n    fetch?:typeof globalThis.fetch;\n}\n\nexport interface RunResult {\n    code:number;\n    error?:Error;\n}\n\nexport function run (argv:string[], io:CliIO):Promise<RunResult>\n```\n\n- `run` never calls `process.exit`, never reads `process.argv`,\n  `process.env`, or `process.cwd()`, and never touches the real terminal.\n  It writes the error (section 2.4) to `io.stderr` itself and returns\n  `{code, error}` so tests can assert on both.\n- Cross-area requirement: every area reached from `run` takes `cwd`,\n  `env`, `signal`, and (for network) `fetch` from a context object passed\n  down, instead of process globals. `git` is run with `execFile(...,\n  {cwd, env})`. Records resolve `.roast/runs` from `io.cwd`. Credentials\n  read `HOME` / `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` from `io.env`.\n- `fetch` defaults to `globalThis.fetch`; tests pass a wrapper that\n  rewrites the URL origin to the fake server while recording the\n  original host (equivalent of Go `redirectDefaultTransport`). Login's\n  loopback callback client uses the real `fetch`.\n- `signal` defaults to a never-aborting signal.\n\n```ts\n// src/cli.ts (entry)\nconst controller = new AbortController()\n// onSignal: first signal aborts, second exits 130 (see below)\nprocess.on('SIGINT', onSignal)\nprocess.on('SIGTERM', onSignal)\nconst { code } = await run(process.argv.slice(2), {\n    stdin: process.stdin,\n    stdout: process.stdout,\n    stderr: process.stderr,\n    env: process.env,\n    cwd: process.cwd(),\n    signal: controller.signal,\n})\n// flush both streams, then exit\nprocess.exit(code)\n```\n\nThe entry waits for stdout/stderr writes to flush (write callback or\n`drain`) before `process.exit`, so piped JSON output is never cut off. It\nalways calls `process.exit`, even on success, so a lingering child or\nhandle cannot hold the process open. An `EPIPE` on stdout is caught by an\n`error` listener on `process.stdout`: it never prints a stack trace and the\nprocess exits quietly with the already computed exit code. A second SIGINT\nor SIGTERM calls `process.exit(130)` directly:\n\n```ts\nlet signalled = false\nconst onSignal = ():void => {\n    if (signalled) process.exit(130)\n    signalled = true\n    controller.abort(new CancelledError())\n}\n```\n\nNode version check: the first statements of `src/cli.ts` compare\n`process.versions.node` with 22.18 (numeric major/minor) and, when lower,\nwrite the error and `process.exit(2)` before any other module is imported\n(dynamic `import()` of the CLI body follows the check).\n\nEvery tool that spawns a process (git runner, `openBrowser`, hook helpers)\ntakes `signal` and kills the child (`SIGTERM`, then `SIGKILL` after a short\ngrace) when it aborts.\n\n### 3.3 Errors\n\n```ts\nexport const ExitCode = {\n    Clean: 0, Findings: 1, Usage: 2, Auth: 3, Partial: 4, Cancelled: 5,\n} as const\n\nexport type ErrorCategory = 'none'|'findings'|'usage'|'auth'|'endpoint'|\n    'resource_limit'|'partial'|'cancelled'\n\nexport class UsageError extends Error {}\nexport class CancelledError extends Error {}  // name 'AbortError'-aware\n// Successful review asking for a non-zero exit (Go gateExit).\nexport class ExitSignal extends Error {\n    constructor (readonly code:1|4) { super(`exit ${code}`) }\n}\n\nexport function errorChainHas (\n    err:unknown,\n    test:(e:Error) => boolean\n):boolean   // walks err, err.cause, ... (cycle-safe)\n\nexport function isCancellation (err:unknown, signal?:AbortSignal):boolean\nexport function exitCode (err:unknown, signal?:AbortSignal):number\nexport function errorCategoryFor (code:number, err:unknown):ErrorCategory\nexport function writeError (\n    out:NodeJS.WritableStream,\n    code:number,\n    err:Error,\n    format:'text'|'json'\n):void\n```\n\n- Wrapping preserves Go message concatenation: `new Error(\\`pin staged\n  tree: ${inner.message}\\`, {cause: inner})`. Category/exit detection\n  walks `cause`.\n- llm area exports its error kinds (auth, endpoint, budget exhausted,\n  work deadline, no final call) as classes or a tagged `kind` property;\n  `errorCategoryFor` imports them.\n- Cancellation: an error in the chain that is a `CancelledError`, or an\n  `AbortError` raised while `io.signal` is aborted with a\n  `CancelledError` reason. A `TimeoutError` from `AbortSignal.timeout`\n  is never cancellation (Go `DeadlineExceeded` is not `Canceled`).\n\n### 3.4 yargs setup\n\n```ts\nyargs(argv)\n    .scriptName('roast')\n    .locale('en')\n    .detectLocale(false)   // English only, whatever LANG/LC_ALL say\n    .parserConfiguration({\n        'boolean-negation': false,   // --no-verify is a real flag\n        'camel-case-expansion': false,\n        'dot-notation': false,\n        'parse-numbers': false,      // ints parsed by our helper\n        'parse-positional-numbers': false,\n        'duplicate-arguments-array': false, // scalar: last wins\n        'strip-aliased': true,\n    })\n    .strict()\n    .exitProcess(false)\n    .fail((msg, err) => { throw err ?? new UsageError(msg) })\n    .option('error-format', { type: 'string', default: 'text',\n        global: true })\n    .version(false)          // custom root-only --version / -v\n    .help('help').alias('help', 'h')\n    .command(['review', '$0'], ..., reviewBuilder, reviewHandler)\n    .command(runsCommand) // ... other areas\n```\n\n- Output capture: parse with the callback form so yargs returns help and\n  error text instead of printing; `run` writes help to `io.stdout`.\n- Root-only `--version`/`-v`: handled in `run` before command dispatch\n  when it is a root-level flag (no subcommand token precedes it); on a\n  subcommand it is an unknown flag.\n- Bare vs explicit review: the handler checks whether the first\n  positional token was `review`; only bare `roast` gets the\n  not-in-a-Git-repository help path (section 2.5).\n- \"Changed\" detection: review flags with a meaningful \"changed\" state\n  (`max-turns`, `deadline`, `request-timeout`, `max-tokens-total`,\n  `max-verified`, `max-attempts`, all `--<role>-*` flags) are declared\n  without a yargs `default`; `undefined` means not changed and the\n  documented default is applied in `review-flags.ts`. Help text states\n  the defaults in the description.\n- All int and duration flags are declared `type: 'string'` and parsed by\n  `parseIntFlag` / `parseGoDuration`; failures are `UsageError`.\n- Slice flags are declared `type: 'string', array: true` and each element\n  is split on plain commas; a test pins `--paths a,b --paths c`. Booleans\n  keep yargs `type: 'boolean'` with `--flag=false` support; `--quick false`\n  is read as a value (accepted difference from Go) and a test pins it.\n- yargs is pinned to English with `.locale('en')` and `.detectLocale(false)`\n  so messages never depend on the environment.\n- `--error-format` validation and the gate bootstrap run in a yargs\n  middleware (or at the top of each handler) after parsing, before the\n  action, in that order. On a parse failure, `run` uses the parsed\n  `--error-format` if yargs produced it, else `text`.\n- Group commands (`gate`, `skill`) register a handler that prints help\n  when there is no subcommand; `.strict()` makes unknown subcommands\n  usage errors.\n\n### 3.5 Review orchestration types\n\n```ts\nexport interface ReviewFlags {\n    config:string; base:string; uncommittedOnly:boolean;\n    staged:boolean; task:string; format:'json'|'markdown'|'both';\n    maxSeverity:string; paths:string[]; exclude:string[];\n    includeVendored:boolean; mode:string; quick:boolean;\n    noVerify:boolean; interactive:boolean; maxTurns?:number;\n    deadlineMs?:number; requestTimeoutMs?:number;\n    maxTokensTotal?:number; maxVerified?:number; maxAttempts?:number;\n    showDropped:boolean; lang:string[]; scope:'diff'|'repo';\n    authorModel:string; finder:RoleFlags; verifier:RoleFlags;\n}\nexport interface RoleFlags {\n    baseUrl?:string; model?:string; protocol?:string;\n    maxOutputTokens?:number;\n}\nexport function validateReviewFlags (f:ReviewFlags):number // gate rank\nexport function runReview (f:ReviewFlags, ctx:RunContext):Promise<void>\nexport function resolveLangs (\n    flags:string[], files:string[], mode:string\n):string[]\nexport function applyRoleFlags (\n    name:'finder'|'verifier', role:ResolvedRole, flags:RoleFlags\n):ResolvedRole\nexport function flagOrConfig<T> (\n    flag:T|undefined, configured:T|undefined, fallback:T\n):T\n```\n\n`runReview` throws `UsageError`, other errors, or `ExitSignal`; it never\nwrites the error itself. Durations are carried in milliseconds as\nnumbers internally; `formatGoDuration(ms)` produces budget strings (Go\nnanosecond precision beyond ms is not needed for flags; config durations\nuse the same parser, see config area). Snapshot cleanup uses\n`try/finally` with a `durable` flag, matching the Go `defer`.\n\nDependencies: config, credentials, trust, scope, context, prompts, llm,\nfinder, verifier, render (incl. textsafe), records, snapshot, gate,\nbuildinfo, duration, `@substrate-system/debug` (`roast:cli`).\n\n### 3.6 Build info\n\nVersion, commit, and build date are injected at build time; from source\nthey are `dev` / `unknown` / `unknown`. esbuild `define`s\n`__ROAST_VERSION__` (from `package.json`),\n`__ROAST_COMMIT__` (`git rev-parse --short=7 HEAD`), `__ROAST_DATE__`\n(`git log -1 --format=%cI`), each falling back to `dev` / `unknown` /\n`unknown` when unavailable. `src/buildinfo.ts` exports them and\n`buildString()`. Tests run unbundled code where the globals are absent:\n`buildinfo.ts` reads them through `typeof` guards.\n\n### 3.7 Test fixtures\n\n- `test/helpers/env.ts`: `cleanEnv(base)` returns a copy of an env with\n  every variable whose upper-cased name starts with `ANTHROPIC_`,\n  `OPENAI_`, `OPENROUTER_`, or `ROAST_` removed. Tests build `io.env`\n  from it (plus `PATH`, `HOME` isolation, and explicit variables); no\n  test mutates `process.env`.\n- `test/helpers/inference-stream.ts`: `writeInferenceStream(res,\n  protocol, response)` turns a complete response object into the native\n  SSE stream for `anthropic`, `responses`, or `chat`, exactly as in\n  section 3.8. `writeJSONStream(res, protocol, body)` parses a JSON\n  string first. Unknown protocol -> error.\n- `test/helpers/run.ts`: `runRoast(args, opts)` wraps `run` with buffer\n  streams, a temp repo cwd, clean env, and an optional redirecting\n  `fetch`; returns `{code, error, stdout, stderr}`.\n- Terminal and browser swaps: `simulateTerminals(t, value)` and\n  `captureBrowser(t)` replace the module-level functions and restore\n  them at test end.\n\n### 3.8 SSE fixture format (`writeInferenceStream`)\n\nSets `Content-Type: text/event-stream`. Each event is\n`[event: <name>\\n]data: <json>\\n\\n`. For `responses`, every emitted\nobject gets `sequence_number` 0, 1, 2, ... in emission order.\n\n- `anthropic`: `message_start` with `message` = response with `content:\n  []`, `stop_reason: null`, `usage` copied with `output_tokens: 0`. For\n  each content block at index i: `content_block_start` (`index`,\n  `content_block` = block with `thinking` and `signature` emptied for\n  thinking, `text` emptied for text, `input: {}` for tool use); deltas\n  (`thinking_delta` + `signature_delta`; `text_delta`; or\n  `input_json_delta` with `partial_json` = JSON of the input);\n  `content_block_stop`. Then `message_delta` (`delta: {stop_reason,\n  stop_sequence: null}`, `usage` = response usage) and `message_stop`.\n  Event name = the object's `type`.\n- `responses`: `response.created` (`response` with `output: []`,\n  `status: in_progress`); per output item: `response.output_item.added`\n  (item with `arguments: \"\"`, `status: in_progress`),\n  `response.function_call_arguments.delta` (`item_id`, `delta` =\n  arguments), `response.function_call_arguments.done` (`arguments`),\n  `response.output_item.done` (full item), each with `output_index`;\n  then `response.completed` with the full response.\n- `chat`: no `event:` lines. Three chunks, each `{id, object:\n  \"chat.completion.chunk\", created: 1, model, choices}`: first, choices\n  with `delta` = message with `tool_calls` re-indexed (`index` = position)\n  and `finish_reason: null`; second, choices with empty `delta` and the\n  real `finish_reason`; third, `choices: []` plus `usage`. Then\n  `data: [DONE]\\n\\n`.\n\n## 4. Deliberate changes\n\n1. The cobra `completion` command is dropped.\n2. Windows is not supported: `openBrowser` uses `open` (darwin) or\n   `xdg-open` (linux) only.\n3. Node `>=22.18`, checked at startup; below it the CLI prints a clear\n   error and exits 2 (spec.md change 3).\n4. Debug tracing via `@substrate-system/debug` namespace `roast:cli`\n   (`DEBUG=roast:*`), never including request/response bodies, headers,\n   prompts, or credentials.\n5. First TypeScript release is `2.0.0`; build info comes from esbuild\n   defines instead of Go ldflags / `debug.ReadBuildInfo`.\n6. Help text wording and layout come from yargs and need not match\n   cobra.\n7. A second SIGINT or SIGTERM force-exits with status 130; Go ignored\n   repeats (spec.md change 22). Ctrl-C (`\\x03`) at a raw-mode secret prompt\n   is cancellation, exit 5.\n8. Accepted yargs parsing differences: decimal-only integers, `--quick\n   false` read as a value, plain comma splitting of list flags (spec.md\n   \"CLI parsing\").\n9. JSON error output is not HTML-escaped; parity is on parsed JSON.\n10. EPIPE on stdout exits quietly with the computed code instead of dying\n    by SIGPIPE.\n11. A parse failure reports in the parsed `--error-format` when yargs\n    produced one, else text.\n\nNot a change: the gate bootstrap's terminal check uses the swappable\n`interactiveTerminals(io.stdin, io.stderr)` instead of Go's direct check\nof the process's stdin/stderr; in production these are the same streams.\n\n## 5. Test plan\n\nAll at the `run(argv, io)` seam with a `node:http` fake inference server\nunless noted. Assert exit codes, JSON, files, and requests; never exact\nhuman-readable text.\n\nExit codes and errors:\n\n- Exit code constants 0..5 (TestExitCodeContract) -- unit.\n- Category mapping for clean, findings, usage, auth, endpoint, budget,\n  cancelled, partial (TestErrorCategoryFor) -- unit on\n  `errorCategoryFor` with wrapped errors.\n- `review --error-format json --format invalid` in a Git repo -> exit 2,\n  stderr parses as `{error_category: \"usage\", exit_code: 2}` with a\n  message (TestJSONErrorOutput).\n- Text error output escapes control bytes (TestWriteErrorEscapesControls)\n  -- unit on `writeError`.\n- Artifact failure wins over the severity gate\n  (TestReviewExitErrorPrefersArtifactFailureOverFindingGate) -- unit.\n- `--max-attempts=0`, `--request-timeout=-1s`, `--max-tokens-total=-1`,\n  `--finder-max-output-tokens=0` with `--quick --uncommitted-only` -> exit\n  2, category usage (TestInvalidResourceOverridesAreUsageErrors).\n- Unknown subcommands and wrong arg counts -> exit 2: `gate bogus`,\n  `config bogus`, `skill bogus`, `runs show` (0 and 2 args), `runs\n  checkout` (0 and 3 args); `gate` and `skill` alone -> exit 0 with help\n  on stdout (TestCommandUsageErrorsExitWithUsageCode).\n- `runs sync`, `runs status` -> exit 2 (TestRunsUploadSubcommandsAreUnknown).\n- New: SIGINT-equivalent abort during the finder -> exit 5, category\n  `cancelled` (signal passed through `io.signal`).\n- New: `--version` exits 0 and prints the build string on stdout.\n- New: a second abort-style signal force-exits 130 -- entry-level test\n  spawning the built CLI against a fake server that never answers, sending\n  SIGINT twice (first alone gives exit 5); no child process remains.\n- New: `\\x03` fed to the raw-mode secret prompt -> cancellation, exit 5\n  (unit on `readSecret` with a fake TTY stream).\n- New: Node below 22.18 -> exit 2 with an error on stderr (unit on the\n  version-check function with injected version strings).\n- New: EPIPE on a closed stdout pipe -> no stack trace, exit code equals\n  the computed code (entry-level test piping into a closed reader).\n- New: parse failure with `--error-format json` parsed -> JSON error;\n  with none parsed -> text.\n- New: `--paths a,b --paths c` splits to three entries; `--max-attempts\n  0x10` -> exit 2; `--quick false` is read as false; JSON error output\n  compared as parsed JSON (message containing `<>&` round-trips).\n- New: empty diff with invalid `--mode` -> exit 0.\n\nCommand surface and help:\n\n- `--help` exits 0 with no config (TestHelpNeedsNoConfiguration).\n- Required commands exist and forbidden ones do not, including no\n  `runs label` (TestPublicCommandSurface) -- assert via running\n  `<cmd> --help` exit codes rather than introspection.\n- Review help states effective defaults (TestReviewHelpShowsEffectiveDefaults)\n  -- keep only as a loose check that the four default numbers appear, or\n  drop as brittle.\n- Bare `roast` outside Git -> exit 0, help on stdout\n  (TestBareCommandOutsideGitShowsHelp).\n- `review --config <file>` outside Git -> exit 2\n  (TestExplicitReviewOutsideGitStillFails).\n- `runs`, `runs prune --dry-run` work in a repo\n  (TestRunsLocalSubcommandsStillWork).\n\nPipeline (end to end with fake server):\n\n- Finder + verifier on a custom endpoint, `--format json --max-severity\n  HIGH` with all budgets 0 and `--max-attempts=1` -> exit 1, confirmed\n  finding in JSON, run bundle and `provider_responses` captured for both\n  roles, meta budgets record 0s / 0 / 1, role meta records profile,\n  protocol, session header; session header sent only by the finder\n  profile; `runs show`, `runs checkout`, `runs` work on the run; only\n  inference requests reach the server\n  (TestFinderVerifierPipelineWithMockEndpoint).\n- Anthropic-protocol finder with chat verifier\n  (TestNativeAnthropicFinderWithChatVerifier).\n- `--scope repo` sends the manifest, uses interactive tools, two finder\n  requests (TestRepositorySurveyUsesManifestAndInteractiveTools).\n- Corpus pinned without a snapshot (no HEAD; `review.snapshot: false`):\n  verifier reads the pinned file, severity canonicalized, exit 1\n  (TestReviewPinsCorpusWithoutSnapshot).\n- Run records live under the Git toplevel even with the config in a\n  subdirectory and cwd deeper (TestRunRecordsLiveUnderProjectToplevel).\n\nSettings resolution:\n\n- Config limits appear in meta budgets and derived meta\n  (TestLimitsInProjectConfigBoundTheReview).\n- `limits.max_diff_bytes` truncates the finder diff\n  (TestMaxDiffBytesInProjectConfigTruncatesTheDiff).\n- `limits.max_prompt_bytes` too small -> exit 2, no request\n  (TestMaxPromptBytesInProjectConfigRejectsALargePrompt).\n- Invalid limits -> non-zero, no request (TestInvalidLimitsAreRejected).\n- Interactive thresholds: small diff downgrades `--interactive`; zero\n  thresholds keep it (TestInteractiveThresholdsInProjectConfig).\n- `review.snapshot` false -> no snapshot, no `refs/roast/` refs\n  (TestReviewSnapshotSettingInProjectConfig).\n- Flags override config for one invocation only, including\n  `--finder-model` (TestFlagsOverrideProjectConfigForOneInvocation).\n- Removed environment variables change nothing (defaults in budgets,\n  no request to env-named endpoints)\n  (TestRemovedEnvironmentVariablesHaveNoEffect).\n- `--author-model` flips the finder; `ROAST_AUTHOR_MODEL` does not\n  (TestAuthorModelFlagSelectsTheFinderFlip,\n  TestAuthorModelEnvironmentDoesNotFlipTheFinder).\n- Role flag credential rules (TestProtocolFlagMovesAnUnmodifiedDefaultEndpoint,\n  TestProtocolFlagClearsWrongProviderCredential,\n  TestBaseURLFlagDoesNotCarryAmbientProviderKey) -- config area unit\n  tests of `OverrideEndpoint`, plus one CLI test that a changed\n  `--finder-base-url` withholds the ambient key.\n- Gate offer: `gate.offer: false` suppresses it without using it up;\n  `ROAST_NO_HOOK` does not suppress it; invalid gate settings -> exit 2\n  (TestGateOfferFalseStopsTheGateOffer,\n  TestNoHookEnvironmentDoesNotStopTheGateOffer,\n  TestInvalidGateSettingsAreRejected). Assert the offer through gate\n  state or a stable marker, not prose.\n\nConfig discovery (CLI level; config area owns details):\n\n- JSONC config used; nearest config below the toplevel; `--config`\n  overrides discovery; invalid config rejected; missing config is a usage\n  error naming `npx roast init`; user config directory not read;\n  `config init --from-url` unknown (TestReviewUsesModelsFromJSONCProjectConfig,\n  TestReviewUsesNearestProjectConfigBelowGitToplevel,\n  TestConfigFlagOverridesDiscoveredProjectConfig,\n  TestReviewRejectsInvalidProjectConfig,\n  TestReviewWithoutProjectConfigNamesRoastInit,\n  TestUserConfigDirectoryIsNotRead, TestConfigInitFromURLIsUnknown).\n- Prompt override paths resolve against the config directory\n  (TestPromptOverrideResolvesAgainstConfigDirectory,\n  TestPromptOverrideFromSubdirectoryWithoutLocalCopy).\n\nTerminal and trust prompt (trust area owns, seam shared):\n\n- Inline trust prompt approves on yes, declined sends nothing,\n  non-terminal fails closed (TestInlineTrustPromptApprovesOnYes,\n  TestInlineTrustPromptDeclinedSendsNothing,\n  TestNonTerminalReviewFailsClosedWithoutPrompting).\n- Default terminal detection rejects non-file streams\n  (TestDefaultTerminalDetectionRejectsNonFiles) -- unit.\n\nLower seams (unit): `parseGoDuration` / `formatGoDuration` round trips\n(`0s`, `45s`, `3m0s`, `1h30m0s`, `1.5ms`), `resolveLangs`,\n`flagOrConfig`, `captureSnapshot` diff pair selection, `cleanEnv`\n(TestClearAmbientEnvironmentUnsetsProviderVariables), `buildString`\nformats (replaces TestResolve, which tested Go toolchain metadata and is\nnot ported), `promptYesDefault` answers including EOF.\n\n## 6. Go baseline references\n\nAt commit `cd08f10`:\n\n- `cmd/roast/main.go`\n- `internal/cli/cli.go`, `internal/cli/config.go`,\n  `internal/cli/prompt.go`\n- `internal/buildinfo/buildinfo.go`, `scripts/build.ts` (ldflags)\n- `internal/testutil/env.go`, `internal/testutil/inference.go`\n- Tests: `internal/cli/cli_test.go`, `settings_test.go`,\n  `project_config_test.go`, `records_test.go`, `hardening_test.go`,\n  `prompt_override_test.go`, `trust_prompt_test.go`, `main_test.go`,\n  `internal/buildinfo/buildinfo_test.go`,\n  `internal/testutil/env_test.go`\n- Behavior read from neighbors: `internal/review/types.go` (severity\n  ranks, `MaxSeverity`), `internal/verify/verify.go` (verifier errors\n  become undecided verdicts), `internal/llm/provider.go` (context error\n  normalization), `internal/scope/scope.go` (`GitRoot`, `Empty`),\n  `internal/config/config.go` (`Gate.Offers`).\n\n## 7. Resolved\n\n1. JSON error output: parity is on parsed JSON, no HTML escaping\n   (spec.md, \"JSON encoding\").\n2. Parse failure uses the parsed `--error-format` when yargs produced one,\n   else text (spec.md, \"CLI parsing\").\n3. Integer flags are decimal only, an accepted yargs difference (spec.md,\n   \"CLI parsing\").\n4. `--quick false` is read as a value by yargs: accepted (spec.md, \"CLI\n   parsing\").\n5. List flags split on plain commas: accepted (spec.md, \"CLI parsing\").\n6. A second Ctrl-C force-exits 130; Ctrl-C at a raw-mode secret prompt is\n   cancellation, exit 5 (spec.md, change 22).\n7. EPIPE on stdout exits quietly with the computed exit code (spec.md,","numLines":520,"startLine":614,"totalLines":1136}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016CmV48WHzBcWSwji1S9RvW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
