g the pipeline will break it, so replace it.\n  - test/cli/require-trust.ts:2 has a comment saying review wiring will be tested with the review command.\n  - Unit tests live in test/review/: classify, find, find-http, fingerprint, fixtures, schema, types, validate."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b283ca8-677a-43f7-a7e2-25611b063cf7","uuid":"3104170a-d852-4ee9-bd6d-80a4f351453c","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:30:35.646Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-20-review-tracer-bullet-chat (TypeScript under src/), I am wiring the `roast review` orchestration in src/cli/review.ts. Read-only task; do not edit anything. I need a compact API reference (exact exported names, full TS signatures including option object fields, and file paths with line numbers) for exactly these functions/types. Quote signatures verbatim; keep prose minimal.\n\n1. src/cli/config.ts: loadProjectConfig and anything it exports; the Config type (from src/config/) fields relevant to: review.excludes, review.snapshot / snapshotEnabled, review.confidence_floor/quick_confidence_floor (and how defaults are obtained), limits.* (max_diff_bytes, max_file_ctx_bytes, max_prompt_bytes, max_total_tokens, max_verified, request_timeout, max_attempts, deadline -- what type are durations stored as?), interactive.min_diff_lines/min_files, prompts.finder_code/finder_prose/verifier, promptPath, credentialEnvNames.\n2. src/config/role.ts + credential.ts + resolved-role.ts: resolveRole, resolveFinderFlip (return shape: note/warning/role), validateRole, overrideEndpoint, updateRole, ResolvedRole fields (profile, baseURL, model, protocol, maxOutputTokens, sessionHeader, apiKey...).\n3. src/cli/trust.ts requireTrust signature and TrustIo.\n4. src/scope/: build (BuildOpts fields), fit, Scope type fields (diff, files, notes, empty?, baseOID, mergeBaseOID, headOID...), gitRoot.\n5. src/context/: pinIndexTree, newQuoteGrounder, buildFileContext, explorationTools, the \"live reader\"/tree type used when no pin (how to make a live Tree), numberedSnippet.\n6. src/prompts/: finder system prompt function, finderUser, verifier system prompt; classifyMode/classifyLangs (wherever they live, maybe src/review/).\n7. src/llm/: createClient (config fields), Ledger/newLedger, the chat send adapter / how a ModelClient is created for a protocol with fetch injection, usage() shape, error classes (auth/endpoint/etc).\n8. src/review/: find() (the finder entrypoint) options and Result type; maxSeverity / severity rank helper.\n9. src/render/: report builder, writeReport (writer), JSON/Markdown render functions, exit mapping helper (the \"exit mapping\" module from ticket 17), Report fields.\n10. src/record/: newRunID, makeRunDir/runs dir resolution, meta writing (writeMeta?), artifact writing (gz), response recorder, finding spill capture, seenBefore, index Record/append, captureEnv, digest helpers, resolveRunDir.\n11. src/runbundle/: build bundle function.\n12. src/cli/errors.ts: UsageError, ExitSignal, CancelledError, exitCode; src/cli/command.ts RunContext fields; src/cli/log.ts.\n13. src/gocompat: parseGoDuration / formatGoDuration names.\n14. test/helpers/*: list each helper file's exports with signatures (run.ts runRoast, inference-server.ts, provider-server.ts, repo.ts, env.ts, terminal.ts, streams.ts), and give one example test file in test/cli/ that uses runRoast + a fake inference server if any exists.\n15. Check whether an existing Go-port-style review test exists anywhere in test/ (grep for 'review' in test/cli and test/helpers).\n\nReturn the reference as one organized list; aim for under ~400 lines total.","agentId":"a0cf7d3e7bd92336b","agentType":"Explore","toolsUsed":["Bash"],"harnessNoteCount":0,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"0dc96b1d36d1021a","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything below was read directly from the source. Before wiring, note these four mismatches with the names and shapes you asked about:\n\n- **The finder's `ground` callback is synchronous, but the grounder is async.** `FindInput.ground` is `Ground = (file, quote) => boolean` (src/review/validate.ts:10). `newQuoteGrounder` returns `Grounder = (file, quote) => Promise<boolean>` (src/context/grounding.ts:16). You can't pass one straight into the other.\n- **`Scope` has no `baseOID` or `mergeBaseOID`.** It has `base`, `headOID` and `stagedTreeOID`. `base_oid` and `merge_base_oid` exist only as fields in `ScopeMeta`. There's also no `empty` field; use `isEmpty(scope)`.\n- **Some names differ from what you listed:** the run ID function is `newRunId` (not `newRunID`), the bundle function is `buildBundle`, and the user prompt renderer is `renderFinderUser`.\n- **Several things don't exist in src/:** a verifier entry point (src/review/ has no verify module), defaults for `interactive.*` (4 and 80 appear only in schema help text), and an exported `ConfigContext` or `Overrides` type.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Config\n\n**src/cli/config.ts**\n- `:14 export const NO_PROJECT_CONFIG`, `:17 export const NO_GATE_CONFIG`\n- `:21 type ConfigContext = Pick<RunContext, 'cwd'|'env'|'signal'>` (not exported)\n- `:31 export async function projectConfigPath (explicit:string, ctx:ConfigContext):Promise<string>`\n- `:49 export function gateConfigPath (repo:string):string`\n- `:53 export async function loadProjectConfig (explicit:string, ctx:ConfigContext):Promise<ProjectConfig>`\n  - Throws `UsageError` when there is no config or it is invalid. It attaches the stored credentials.\n\n**src/config/load.ts**\n- `:120 export interface ProjectConfig extends NormalizedConfig { readonly dir:string; readonly stored?:StoredCredentials; }`\n- `:108 NormalizedConfig`:\n  - `review: NonNullable<RawConfig['review']> & { confidence_floor:number; quick_confidence_floor:number; }`\n  - `limits?: NormalizedLimits`\n  - `prompts?`, `interactive?`, `gate?` are raw schema types\n- `:101 NormalizedLimits`: same as the raw limits, except `deadline?:GoDuration; request_timeout?:GoDuration;`\n  - **Durations are stored as `bigint` nanoseconds.** Convert with `toMillis`.\n  - The two duration keys are deleted when unset.\n- Raw schema (src/config/schema.ts:92):\n  - `review`: `{confidence_floor?, quick_confidence_floor?, excludes?:string[], snapshot?:boolean}`\n  - `prompts`: `{finder_code?, finder_prose?, verifier?: string}`\n  - `limits`: `{deadline?, request_timeout? (Go duration strings), max_total_tokens?, max_diff_bytes?, max_prompt_bytes?, max_file_ctx_bytes?, max_attempts?, max_verified?: number}`\n  - `interactive`: `{min_files?, min_diff_lines?: number}`\n- **Floor defaults** are filled in by `normalize` (`:461`) as `review.confidence_floor || DEFAULT_CONFIDENCE_FLOOR`. After loading they are always set.\n- **Limits defaults** are not applied. Read them yourself from `DEFAULT_LIMITS`.\n- `:530 export function promptPath (cfg:ProjectConfig, p:string):string` resolves relative paths against `cfg.dir`.\n- `:536 export function credentialEnvNames (cfg:ProjectConfig):string[]`\n- `:542 export function snapshotEnabled (cfg:ProjectConfig):boolean` returns `review.snapshot ?? DEFAULT_SNAPSHOT`.\n- `:40 export class ConfigError extends Error`\n\n**src/config/defaults.ts**\n- `DEFAULT_CONFIDENCE_FLOOR = 0.6`\n- `DEFAULT_QUICK_CONFIDENCE_FLOOR = 0.8`\n- `DEFAULT_SNAPSHOT = true`\n- `:10 DEFAULT_LIMITS = {deadline:'10m', request_timeout:'10m', max_total_tokens:3_000_000, max_diff_bytes:1_000_000, max_prompt_bytes:8_000_000, max_file_ctx_bytes:400_000, max_attempts:4, max_verified:25}`\n  - The durations here are strings and must be parsed with `parseGoDuration`.\n\n## 2. Roles and credentials\n\n**src/config/role.ts**\n- `:21 export type RoleName = 'finder'|'verifier'`\n- `:65 export function resolveRole (cfg:ProjectConfig, name:RoleName, env:Env):ResolvedRole` (throws `ConfigError`)\n- `:77 export interface FlipResult { role:ResolvedRole; note?:string; warn?:string; }` (the field is `warn`, not `warning`)\n- `:93 export function resolveFinderFlip (cfg:ProjectConfig, finder:ResolvedRole, authorModel:string, env:Env):FlipResult`\n- `:202 export function validateRole (name:string, role:ResolvedRole):void` (throws `ConfigError`)\n- `:157 isPlaceholderModel(model)`, `:163 validateEndpoint(field, baseURL, ...)`\n- `:19` re-exports `type ResolvedRole, updateRole`\n\n**src/config/resolved-role.ts**\n- `:5 ResolvedRole`, all fields readonly:\n  - `profile`, `baseURL`, `apiKey` (non-enumerable), `model`, `protocol`: `string`\n  - `maxOutputTokens: number`\n  - `sessionHeader: string`\n  - `pin: boolean`\n  - `authorRoutes: Readonly<Record<string,string>>`\n  - `credential: CredentialSource`\n  - `explicitEndpoint: boolean`\n  - `stored?: StoredCredentials` (non-enumerable)\n- `:34 export function updateRole (role:ResolvedRole, changes:Partial<ResolvedRole>):ResolvedRole`. Use this instead of a spread, which drops `apiKey`.\n\n**src/config/credential.ts**\n- `:13 export type Env = Readonly<Record<string, string|undefined>>`\n- `:231 export function overrideEndpoint (roleName:string, role:ResolvedRole, overrides:Overrides, env:Env):ResolvedRole`\n  - `Overrides` (`:166`, not exported) is `{ baseURL?:string; protocol?:string }`. Pass `undefined` for a flag that wasn't given.\n\n## 3. Trust (src/cli/trust.ts)\n- `:34 export type TrustIo = Pick<RunContext, 'stdin'|'stderr'|'lines'|'env'|'signal'>`\n- `:66 export async function requireTrust (dir:string, cfg:ProjectConfig, io:TrustIo):Promise<void>`\n  - Throws `UsageError(NOT_APPROVED | LEGACY_APPROVAL)`. Asks interactively only when attached to terminals.\n\n## 4. Scope (src/scope/index.ts re-exports build, fit, isEmpty, BuildOpts, Scope, ScopeKind, SizeEntry, DEFAULT_IGNORES, gitRoot)\n\n**src/scope/build.ts**\n- `:30 export type ScopeKind = ''|'diff'|'repo'`\n- `:32 BuildOpts`:\n  ```ts\n  { base?:string; uncommittedOnly?:boolean; stagedOnly?:boolean; paths?:readonly string[]; excludes?:readonly string[]; includeVendored?:boolean; scope?:string; stagedTreeOID?:string; maxFileDiffBytes?:number; env?:NodeJS.ProcessEnv }\n  ```\n- `:47 Scope` (all readonly):\n  ```ts\n  { diff:string; diffBytes:Buffer; files:readonly string[]; base:string; notes:readonly string[]; staged:boolean; stagedTreeOID:string; manifest:string; survey:boolean; headOID:string }\n  ```\n- `:66 export function isEmpty (scope:Scope):boolean`\n- `:171 export async function build (repo:string, opts:BuildOpts, signal?:AbortSignal):Promise<Scope>`\n- `:407 export function fit (scope:Scope, maxBytes:number):{ scope:Scope, breakdown:SizeEntry[]|null }`\n- `:106 resolveBase`, `:121 buildRangeArgs`, `:382 fileDiffBytes(diff:Buffer, path:string):number`\n\n**src/git/git.ts**\n- `:126 export async function gitRoot (start:string, opts:GitRunOpts = {}):Promise<string>`\n- `GitRunOpts` (`:22`): `{signal?, env?, extraEnv?, ...}`\n\n## 5. Context\n- **src/context/tree.ts**\n  - `:9 export type Tree = { readonly oid:string; readonly worktree:boolean }`\n  - `:16 export const LIVE_TREE:Tree` (`{oid:'', worktree:false}`). This is the live tree to use when nothing is pinned.\n  - `pinned(t)`, `staged(t)`, `pinnedWorktree(oid):Tree`\n  - `:62 export async function pinIndexTree (repo:string, signal:AbortSignal, opts:Omit<ContextOpts,'signal'> = {}):Promise<Tree>`\n- **src/context/grounding.ts**\n  - `:16 export type Grounder = (file:string, quote:string) => Promise<boolean>`\n  - `:336 export function newQuoteGrounder (repo:string, tree:Tree, diff:Buffer, opts:ContextOpts = {}):Grounder`. `diff` is the scope's diff before `fit`.\n- **src/context/snippet.ts**\n  - `:14 FILE_SNIPPET_BYTES = 120000`\n  - `:112 export async function numberedSnippet (repo:string, relpath:string, maxBytes:number, tree:Tree, opts:ContextOpts = {}):Promise<string>`\n  - `:180 export async function buildFileContext (repo:string, files:readonly string[], budget:number, tree:Tree, opts:ContextOpts = {}):Promise<string>`\n- **src/context/tools.ts**\n  - `:57 export function explorationTools (repo:string, tree:Tree, opts:Omit<ContextOpts,'signal'> = {}):Tool[]`\n- **src/context/git.ts**\n  - `:7 ContextOpts` (has `signal?` and `env?`)\n\n## 6. Prompts and classification\n- **src/prompts/index.ts**\n  - `:19 export async function finderSystem (mode:string, scope:string, quick:boolean, langs:ReadonlyArray<string>, overridePath:string):Promise<string>`\n    - `scope` is `'repo'` for a survey, otherwise diff. `overridePath` is `''` for the built-in prompt.\n  - `:51 export async function verifierSystem (overridePath:string):Promise<string>`\n- **src/prompts/render.ts**\n  - `:6 FinderUserVars = { task:string; survey:boolean; diff:string; fileContext:string; manifest:string }`\n  - `:27 export function renderFinderUser (v:Readonly<FinderUserVars>):string`\n  - `:15 VerifierVars = { severity, file, lines, description, codeQuote, fixedCode, fileSnippet: string; confidence:number }`\n  - `:73 renderVerifierUser(v)`\n  - `:117 dataText(text)`\n- **src/review/classify.ts**\n  - `:28 export function classifyMode (files:string[]):'code'|'prose'|'mixed'`\n  - `:43 export function classifyLangs (files:string[]):string[]`\n  - `:60 export function resolveLangs (values:string[], files:string[], mode:string):string[]`\n\n## 7. LLM\n- **src/llm/types.ts**\n  - `:3 Protocol = 'chat'|'responses'|'anthropic'`\n  - `:14 ClientConfig`:\n    ```ts\n    { role:string; baseUrl:string; apiKey:string; model:string; protocol:''|Protocol; maxOutputTokens:number; maxAttempts:number; requestTimeoutMs:number; sessionHeader?:string; captureResponse?:(raw:RawResponse)=>Promise<void>|void; fetch?:typeof globalThis.fetch }\n    ```\n  - `:5 RawResponse = { role; protocol:Protocol; model; contentType:'application/json'|'text/event-stream'; body:Uint8Array }`\n  - `:75 Usage = { uncachedInputTokens; cachedInputTokens; cacheWriteTokens; outputTokens; calls }` (camelCase)\n  - `:140 RecordUsage`: the same fields in snake_case (`uncached_input_tokens` and so on)\n  - `:149 Client = { readonly name:string; converse<T>(system, user, opts:ConverseOptions<T>, signal); completeStructured<T>(system, user, schemaName, result, signal); usage():RecordUsage }`\n- **src/llm/client.ts**\n  - `:38 ModelClient = { config; protocol; maxAttempts; send(req); requestBytes(req); usage():Usage }`\n  - `:165 export function createModelClient (config:ClientConfig):ModelClient`. It picks the protocol adapter, and fetch is injected through `config.fetch`. It throws if `maxOutputTokens` is not above 0 or the API key is empty.\n  - `:268 CreateClientOptions = { ledger?:Ledger|null; now?:()=>number; sleep?:Sleep; sessionId?:()=>string }`\n  - `:289 export function createClient (model:ModelClient, opts:CreateClientOptions = {}):Client`\n- **src/llm/http.ts**\n  - `setFetch(f)`, `resetFetch()`, `currentFetch()`. These are module-level fallbacks.\n- **src/llm/ledger.ts**\n  - `:27 class Ledger`, with methods `reserve`, `exhausted`, `outstanding`, `committed():{spent,limit}`\n  - `:76 export function newLedger (limit:number):Ledger|null` (returns null when `limit <= 0`)\n- **src/llm/errors.ts**\n  - `LlmError` (`:65`, has `.kind:LlmErrorKind`)\n  - `AuthError`, `EndpointError`, `BudgetExhaustedError`, `WorkDeadlineError`, `NoFinalCallError`. Each is built with `(message:string, options?:LlmErrorOptions)`.\n  - `ProviderError` (`:138`), `IncompleteStreamError`, `CaptureError`\n  - `:225 hasSentinel(err, s:Sentinel)`, where `Sentinel = 'no-final-call'|'work-deadline'|'budget-exhausted'|'auth'|'endpoint'`\n- **src/llm/agent.ts**\n  - `DEFAULT_MAX_TURNS = 8`, `DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 4`\n- **src/llm/session.ts**\n  - `:8 newSessionId():string`\n\n## 8. Review\n- **src/review/find.ts**\n  - `:13 FindInput`:\n    ```ts\n    { system:string; user:string; quick?:boolean; confidenceFloor:number; interactive?:boolean; tools?:readonly Tool[]; maxTurns?:number; survey?:boolean; ground?:Ground; capture?:(finding:WireFinding)=>void; deadline?:number /* abs ms epoch */ }\n    ```\n  - `:74 export async function find (client:Client, input:FindInput, signal:AbortSignal):Promise<Result>`\n    - Without `interactive` it makes one `completeStructured` call. With `interactive` it runs `converse` with tools.\n- **src/review/types.ts**\n  - `:56 Result = { findings:Finding[]; dropped:Finding[]; assessment:string; notes:string[]; incomplete?:boolean; stopReason?:string }`\n  - `SEVERITIES = ['INFO','LOW','MEDIUM','HIGH','CRITICAL']`\n  - `:10 severityRank(severity:string):number` (an unknown severity maps to 0)\n  - `:15 parseSeverity(value):Severity|null`\n  - `:97 effectiveSeverity(f)`\n  - `:105 export function maxSeverity (result:Pick<Result,'findings'>):number` (returns -1 when there are no findings)\n- **src/review/validate.ts**\n  - `:10 Ground = (file, quote) => boolean`\n  - `:12 validate(resp, confidenceFloor, ground?):Result`\n\n## 9. Render\n- **src/render/render.ts**\n  - `:10 Report`:\n    ```ts\n    { result:Omit<Result,'notes'>&{notes?:string[]|null}; mode:string; filesReviewed?:string[]|null; task?:string; runId?:string; budgets?:Record<string,unknown>|null; quick?:boolean; verified?:boolean; diffTruncated?:boolean; originalDiffBytes?:number; sizeBreakdown?:SizeEntry[]|null; usage?:Record<string,RecordUsage>|null; prior?:Map<string,string>|null; promptPacks?:string[]|null; reviewKind?:''|'survey_triage'; completion?:string; manifestFileCount?:number; stopReason?:string }\n    ```\n  - `:90 toJSON(r:Report):string`\n  - `:125 toMarkdown(r:Report, showDropped:boolean):string`\n- **src/render/write.ts**\n  - `:5 export function writeReport (io:{ stdout:Writable; stderr:Writable }, format:'json'|'markdown'|'both', showDropped:boolean, report:Report):void`\n  - JSON goes to stdout and Markdown to stderr.\n- **src/render/exit.ts** (the exit-mapping module)\n  - `:4 export function reportExitCode (result:Pick<Result,'findings'>, gateRank:number, partial:boolean):number`\n  - Returns 1 if a non-refuted finding has rank `>= gateRank` (and `gateRank >= 0`). Otherwise returns 4 when `partial`, else 0.\n\n## 10. Record\n- **run-id.ts**\n  - `:4 newRunId():string`, formatted like `20261123T120000Z-abcd1234`\n- **dir.ts**\n  - `STATE_DIR = '.roast'`\n  - `:77 recordDir(cwd, opts:GitRunOpts={}):Promise<string>`, which resolves to `<toplevel>/.roast/runs` (or `''`)\n  - `:37 makeRunDir(dir, runId):Promise<string>`\n  - `ensureDir`, `isValidName`, `NoRecordDirError`\n- **meta.ts**\n  - `:23 resolveRunDir(dir, id):Promise<string>`\n  - `:47 writeMeta(dir, meta:Meta):Promise<string>`\n  - `:62 readMeta(dir, id)`\n  - `:72 writeArtifact(dir, runId, name, content:string|Uint8Array):Promise<string>` (writes `name.gz`)\n  - `:86 readArtifact(runDir, name)`\n  - `:95 writeReport(dir, runId, markdown)` writes `report.md`. It shares a name with the render `writeReport`, so alias one on import.\n  - Re-exports `serializeMeta`, `wireProtocol`, `captureEnv`, `digest`, plus all meta types\n- **meta-json.ts**\n  - `:47 captureEnv(env:NodeJS.ProcessEnv, extraSecrets:readonly string[]=[]):string[]`\n  - `:57 digest(x:string|Uint8Array):string` (sha256 hex)\n  - `:43 wireProtocol(role:RoleMeta)`\n- **meta-types.ts**\n  - `Meta = {run_id, replay_of?, ts, repo, invoke_dir?, argv?, roast:BuildMeta, scope:ScopeMeta, derived:DerivedMeta, roles:Record<string,RoleMeta>, snapshot:SnapshotMeta, digests:DigestMeta, budgets?, usage?:Record<string,UsageMeta>, env_names_only?, caveats?}`\n  - `ScopeMeta`: kind, base, uncommitted_only, staged_only, include_vendored, paths, excludes, base_oid, merge_base_oid, head_oid, survey, staged, files\n  - `DerivedMeta`: mode, langs?, quick?, interactive, max_turns, confidence_floor, do_verify, task?, max_severity?, max_diff_bytes?, max_file_ctx_bytes?\n  - `RoleMeta`: profile?, base_url, model, protocol, api?, max_output_tokens, session_header?, prompt_digest?\n  - `SnapshotMeta`: `{captured:boolean; reason?; ref?; commit?; ...}`\n  - `DigestMeta`: `{input_kind, input, input_bytes, system_prompt?, user_prompt?}`\n- **responses.ts**\n  - `class ResponseRecorder { constructor(dir:string, runId:string); append(role, protocol, model, contentType, body:Uint8Array):Promise<void> }`\n  - `PROVIDER_RESPONSES_FILE`\n- **findings.ts**\n  - `:8 FindingSink = (finding:WireFinding) => Promise<void>`\n  - `:10 openFindingSpill(dir, runId):Promise<FindingSink|null>` (writes `findings.jsonl`)\n- **index-file.ts**\n  - `:14 appendRunLine(dir, report:Report, repo, argv:readonly string[]|null, now=new Date()):Promise<void>`\n  - `:65 seenBefore(dir, repoDir, findings:readonly Finding[], lookbackFiles=3):Promise<Map<string, PriorSighting>>`\n  - `PriorSighting = { runTS:string; dropReason:string }`\n\n## 11. Run bundle (src/runbundle/bundle.ts)\n- `:48 Bundle = { path:string, sha256:string, size:number }`\n- `:50 export function buildBundle (runDir:string):Bundle` (synchronous)\n- `:253 verifyBundle(filePath)`\n- `BUNDLE_FILE = 'bundle.tar.zst'`, `BundleBuildInProgressError`\n\n## 12. CLI plumbing\n- **src/cli/errors.ts**\n  - `ExitCode = {Clean:0, Findings:1, Usage:2, Auth:3, Partial:4, Cancelled:5}`\n  - `UsageError(message, options?)`\n  - `CancelledError(message='cancelled', options?)`\n  - `ExitSignal(code:1|4)` with `.code`\n  - `:87 exitCode(err:unknown, signal?:AbortSignal):number`\n  - `errorCategoryFor`, `writeError`, `isCancellation`, `errorChainHas`\n- **src/cli/command.ts:10 RunContext**:\n  ```ts\n  { stdin; stdout; stderr; env:Readonly<Record<string,string|undefined>>; cwd:string; signal:AbortSignal; fetch:typeof globalThis.fetch; lines:LineReader; errorFormat:ErrorFormat; path:string[]; rootHelp():Promise<string> }\n  ```\n  - `CommandDef = {command, describe, builder?:(y:Argv)=>Argv, handler?:(args:CommandArgs, ctx:RunContext)=>void|Promise<void>, subcommands?}`\n- **src/cli/log.ts:5**\n  - `export function logf (out:NodeJS.WritableStream, message:string):void` writes `roast: <sanitized>\\n`\n- **src/cli/review.ts** is currently a 40-line stub. `reviewCommand` uses `command:['review','$0']`; inside a repo it throws `UsageError('review is not implemented yet...')`.\n\n## 13. Durations (src/gocompat/duration.ts)\n- `type GoDuration = bigint` (nanoseconds)\n- `:36 parseGoDuration(orig:string):GoDuration`\n- `:118 toMillis(ns):number`\n- `:133 formatGoDuration(d):string`\n- `:108 isGoDuration(s)`\n\n## 14. Test helpers (test/helpers/)\n- **run.ts**\n  - `RunRoastOpts {cwd?, env?:Record<string,string>, stdin?:ReadableStream|string, signal?, redirectTo?:string}`\n  - `RunRoastResult extends RunResult {stdout, stderr, hosts:string[]}`, where `RunResult = {code:number; error?:Error}`\n  - `runRoast(args:string[], opts={}):Promise<RunRoastResult>`\n  - `redirectingFetch(origin, hosts)`\n- **inference-server.ts**\n  - `RecordedRequest {method, path, headers, body, ...}`\n  - `Reply = {stream:unknown, protocol?} | {status, headers?, body?}`\n  - `Script = (req, n) => Reply`\n  - `InferenceServer {url, requests, close()}`\n  - `startInferenceServer(script):Promise<InferenceServer>`\n  - `protocolForPath(path)`\n- **inference-stream.ts**\n  - `writeInferenceStream(res, protocol, response)`, `writeJSONStream(res, protocol, body)`\n- **provider-server.ts**\n  - `providerServer(inference?:Script)` returns `{...InferenceServer, credentials:string[], hooks:{answerModels, answerKey}}`\n- **repo.ts**\n  - `TempDir {dir, env, remove()}`\n  - `isolatedEnv(root)`, `tempDir(prefix?)`, `tempRepo(prefix?)` (runs `git init`)\n- **env.ts**\n  - `cleanEnv(base):Record<string,string>`\n- **terminal.ts**\n  - `simulateTerminals(t, value:boolean)`, `captureBrowser(t, error?):string[]`\n- **streams.ts**\n  - `class BufferStream extends Writable` (with `.text()`), `inputStream(text='')`\n- **test.ts**\n  - `test(name, fn:(t:CleanupTest)=>...)`, where `CleanupTest` has `cleanup(fn)`\n- **spawn.ts**\n  - `ROOT`, `run(command, args, opts)`\n- **doctor-probe.ts**\n  - `probeCall`, `doctorProbe():Script`\n\n**Example of `runRoast` with a fake inference server:** test/cli/doctor.ts\n- `:45-58` has the `doctor()` wrapper, which runs `providerServer(doctorProbe())` and `runRoast([...], {cwd, env, redirectTo:server.url})`.\n- `:253+` starts `startInferenceServer`, writes `.roast.json` with `endpoint: server.url + ...`, then runs `approveDoctorConfig`.\n- The finder-only pattern, calling `find` against a real HTTP fake through `createModelClient` and `createClient`, is in test/review/find-http.ts.\n\n## 15. Existing review tests\n- There is no review pipeline test in the style of the Go port.\n- test/cli/run.ts:105, `'review inside a repository is not available yet'`, asserts exit 2. Wiring the pipeline will break it, so replace it.\n- test/cli/require-trust.ts:2 has a comment saying review wiring will be tested with the review command.\n- Unit tests live in test/review/: classify, find, find-http, fingerprint, fixtures, schema, types, validate."}],"resolvedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","totalDurationMs":124708,"totalTokens":90555,"totalToolUseCount":20,"usage":{"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":126},"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1569,"cache_read_input_tokens":79063,"output_tokens":9921,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1569},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9921,"cache_read_input_tokens":79063,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1569,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1569,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"toolStats":{"readCount":0,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":20,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0},"canContinueAgent":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013ZjZWsp3co15WosgrPTPBD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
