{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jq6ikWXX3Lv4PZ3L6unmpE","type":"tool_result","content":"# Run records\n\n- Resolve the records directory once with `recordDir(cwd, { env })` and\n  pass it into record operations. An empty directory means recording is\n  unavailable; checked writes throw `NoRecordDirError`, while the index\n  and finding spill remain best effort. Filesystem APIs are asynchronous.\n- Validate run IDs and artifact names before any filesystem operation.\n  `makeRunDir` tightens both private directories on each write;\n  `openPrivate` tightens file descriptors, including existing files.\n- `meta-types.ts`, ordered field lists in `meta-json.ts`, and decoding in\n  `meta-read.ts` must change together when the metadata contract changes.\n  Optional fields serialize with Go omitempty behavior. Readers ignore\n  unknown exact-case keys and provide zero values for absent/null fields.\n- Metadata uses the specified fixed `meta.json.tmp` staging path and\n  rename. Tighten a leftover staging file before publishing it. The\n  general fsutil atomic helper uses random exclusive temporary files,\n  so it does not provide this legacy staging-file behavior.\n- Diff input stays bytes through hashing and gzip. Provider JSON body\n  compaction is textual; parsing and re-encoding loses numeric spellings\n  and duplicate keys. JSON escaping follows the spec index.\n- Map keys sort with `compareBytes`. Preserve struct field order instead\n  of recursively sorting whole metadata or finding objects. The monthly\n  index uses local timestamps; metadata and finding spill use UTC.\n- Await recorder and spill writes. Their per-instance queues serialize\n  concurrent appends; response appends also fsync before returning.\n- Record tests use `test/record/repo.ts` to chdir into a temporary Git\n  repository and isolate home/config directories. Never write this\n  checkout's self-ignored `.roast/`. Import tests in `test/record/index.ts`,\n  which is imported by `test/index.ts`.\n# Report rendering\n\n- Test rendering directly in `test/render/`; import new test modules\n  from `test/index.ts`. The review command owns flag validation and\n  finalization errors.\n- JSON preserves raw strings. Only Markdown goes through `textsafe`.\n  Build finding, verdict and usage objects explicitly to preserve their\n  field order; sort top-level keys and nested budget keys separately.\n- Report usage consumes the client's `RecordUsage` (snake-case fields),\n  rather than the protocol adapter's internal `Usage`.\n- Preserve absent vs empty collections. Use `deepEqual`, rather than\n  tapzero's loose `equal`, when checking null versus undefined.\n- Markdown rendering is pure. Stream writes live in `write.ts`, exported\n  through `render.ts`; keep JSON before Markdown when writing both.\n# TypeScript rewrite\n\nApplies to `src/`, `test/`, and `scripts/`. Notes for one area are in\nthat area's file (index in `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Tooling\n\n- `npm test` runs `typecheck`, then bundles and runs the tapzero suite.\n  A new test module must be imported from `test/index.ts`. esbuild drops\n  unused imports without resolving them, so only `typecheck` catches a\n  broken import.\n- `npm run test:one -- test/<area>/<file>.ts` bundles one test module\n  to `test/one-bundle.js` and runs it through tap-spec. Test modules\n  cannot run directly under Node: their `.js` import specifiers only\n  resolve once bundled. It does not typecheck; run `typecheck` too.\n- Lint with `npm run lint`: it preloads `scripts/eslint-ts6.ts`, which\n  gives eslint the TypeScript 6 API because typescript-eslint throws on\n  the TypeScript 7 that `typecheck` uses.\n- Legacy launcher and release files are excluded by name from lint (the\n  `--ignore-pattern` list) and typecheck (`tsconfig.json` `exclude`);\n  the launcher compiles with `tsconfig.launcher.json`.\n- Node runs `scripts/` directly (type stripping), so they use only\n  erasable syntax: no enums, namespaces, or parameter properties.\n- `baseOptions` in `scripts/esbuild-options.ts` holds the esbuild\n  options every bundle shares (text loaders for `.tmpl`, `.md`, `.sh`;\n  `mainFields: ['module', 'main']`, which `jsonc-parser`'s UMD build\n  needs); `scripts/bundle.ts` adds the `require` shim banner. A test\n  that bundles code itself uses both.\n- `npm run bundle` also writes `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`\n  (`scripts/licenses.ts`) and fails, naming the package, when a bundled\n  package lacks an allowlisted `license` field or a license file. A new\n  runtime dependency must pass it; extending `ALLOWED_LICENSES` needs\n  maintainer approval. `@substrate-system/debug` fails it today, so no\n  `src/` module may import it yet.\n\n## Source conventions\n\n- Keep source ASCII: write `\\uXXXX` escapes. Some editing tools decode\n  escapes into literal characters when writing; check with\n  `grep -nP '[^\\x00-\\x7f]'` after writing a file. eslint `--fix`\n  (quote-props) rewrites a quoted `'\\u00e9'` object key into a literal\n  non-ASCII identifier; put such keys in a const and use a computed key.\n- eslint rejects control characters in regex literals\n  (`no-control-regex`) and labeled statements (`no-labels`); scan char\n  codes and use helper functions instead.\n- Startup guards live in `src/startup.ts`, not `src/cli.ts`: importing\n  the entry runs the CLI, so testable helpers sit in other modules.\n- Module-level swappable functions use a mutable hooks object plus a\n  delegating export (`terminalHooks`, `skillHooks.lookPath`), because\n  tests cannot reassign an ESM `let` export. Swap the object's field\n  and restore it in `t.cleanup`.\n- Shared helpers; import these, never re-implement:\n  `src/gocompat/` (`strings.ts`: Go TrimSpace/Ext/`%.2f`/strconv.Quote/\n  byte-order sort and `truncateUtf8`; `duration.ts`: Go durations as\n  bigint nanoseconds; `match.ts`: Go `path.Match`),\n  `src/textsafe/textsafe.ts`, `src/fsutil/atomic.ts`\n  (`writeFileAtomic`, options cover trust, credentials, and gate temp\n  names and error messages), `src/git/git.ts` (the only git runner;\n  pass the CLI context's `env`, it reads `process.env` only when none is\n  given), `src/util/pool.ts` (`mapPool`).\n\n## CLI core (`src/cli/`)\n\n- Commands are `CommandDef`s (`command.ts`) listed in `commands.ts`;\n  `run.ts` builds the yargs tree from that list plus `registerCommand`\n  (tests), and calls the handler only after parsing succeeds.\n- A handler gets a `RunContext` (cwd, env, signal, fetch, one shared\n  `LineReader`) and throws `UsageError` / `ExitSignal` / any error; it\n  never writes the error itself or reads process globals.\n- A group with `subcommands` and no handler prints its help.\n- Terminal detection and browser opening are swapped through\n  `terminalHooks` (`terminal.ts`).\n- With only the default `$0` command registered, yargs omits the\n  Commands section from root help; it appears once a second command\n  registers.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Use the `test` wrapper in `test/helpers/test.ts`, which adds Go-style\n  `t.cleanup` (tapzero has no teardown hook). tapzero's `Test` has no\n  `notOk`; write `t.ok(!x, ...)`.\n- CLI tests run in-process with `runRoast` (`test/helpers/run.ts`),\n  which makes a temp repo with an isolated env (`test/helpers/repo.ts`:\n  `tempRepo`, `tempDir`, which also sets `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`).\n  `test/cli/process.ts` spawns `dist/cli.js`, so it needs a fresh\n  `npm run bundle` (`npm test` does that).\n- Swap terminals and the browser with `simulateTerminals` /\n  `captureBrowser` (`test/helpers/terminal.ts`).\n- Tests that spawn processes use `test/helpers/spawn.ts` (`ROOT`,\n  `run`).\n- Git runner tests observe a child by putting a fake `git` shell script\n  first on the injected `PATH` (spawn resolves the command through\n  `env.PATH`); see `test/git/git.ts`.\n- Live tests live under `test/live/` (entry `index.ts`,\n  `npm run test:live`); each passes with a \"skipped\" note when its\n  `ROAST_LIVE_*` key is unset, so the TAP stream is never empty.\n\n## Differential harness (`test/diff/`, deleted at M6)\n\n- `npm run test:diff` runs the harness self-tests (no Go needed), then\n  every scenario against the Go baseline built at `cd08f10` into\n  `node_modules/.cache/roast-diff/` (delete it to force a rebuild).\n  Without `go` on `PATH` every scenario is a TAP skip.\n- Add a milestone's scenarios as a `Scenario[]` under\n  `test/diff/scenarios/` and list it in `SCENARIOS` (`index.ts`);\n  `server`, `records`, and `requests` turn on the fake server and\n  record/request comparison.\nsrc/record/run-id.ts:4:export function newRunId ():string {\nsrc/record/json.ts:2:export { compareBytes } from '../gocompat/strings.js'\nsrc/record/json.ts:5:export function goStringify (value:unknown, indent?:number):string {\nsrc/record/json.ts:11:export function compactJSON (text:string):string {\nsrc/record/json.ts:34:export function encodeResponseBody (\nsrc/record/json.ts:56:export function rfc3339NanoUTC (d:Date):string {\nsrc/record/json.ts:61:export function rfc3339Local (d:Date):string {\nsrc/record/json.ts:73:export function sortedMap (value:unknown):unknown {\nsrc/record/dir.ts:8:export const STATE_DIR = '.roast'\nsrc/record/dir.ts:10:export class NoRecordDirError extends Error {\nsrc/record/dir.ts:17:export function isValidName (name:string):boolean {\nsrc/record/dir.ts:22:export async function ensureDir (dir:string):Promise<void> {\nsrc/record/dir.ts:37:export async function makeRunDir (\nsrc/record/dir.ts:51:export async function openPrivate (\nsrc/record/dir.ts:65:export async function writePrivate (\nsrc/record/dir.ts:77:export async function recordDir (","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b283ca8-677a-43f7-a7e2-25611b063cf7","uuid":"6e384260-e409-47ce-86df-4ad497b6b39e","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:31:02.657Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Run records\n\n- Resolve the records directory once with `recordDir(cwd, { env })` and\n  pass it 