{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLuotNeAPz5wpmUht62X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] lint, typecheck, and the TS test suite pass, and the Go build and Go tests still pass.\n\n`npx roast review --no-verify` (and bare `npx roast --no-verify`) now runs end to end on a `chat` provider, and every checklist item is checked off. `npm test` passed 6587/6587, lint is clean, and `go build ./...` and `npm run test:go` pass. Everything is committed in 8 commits; only `.redeye/notes.md` is left out, as instructed.\n\n**What was built**\n- **Orchestration** (`src/cli/review.ts`): `runReview` covers spec 2.8 steps 1–16 and 19–21, plus `reviewExitError`. Step 17 (verification) passes the finder result through unchanged until ticket 21. The gate offer is an empty call at the top of the handler for ticket 30. Snapshot functions can be swapped in through `reviewHooks.snapshot` for ticket 22.\n- **Flags** (`src/cli/review-flags.ts`): definitions, value parsing (decimal integers, Go durations) and the 2.7 validation rules.\n- **Helpers**: `src/cli/resolve.ts` (the flag/config/default helpers and `applyRoleFlags`) and `src/cli/snapshot-meta.ts` (`captureSnapshot`; until ticket 22 the default capture fails, so the run records `captured: false` and continues).\n- **Test helpers**: `test/helpers/review.ts`, with `settingsRepo`, `approveProjectConfig`, `requestRecorder` and `reviewMeta`.\n\n**Changes outside the listed files**\n- **`argv` added to `RunContext`.** yargs keeps only the last `--paths`, so the review re-reads list flags from the original arguments. The run record needs the raw arguments too.\n- **The finder accepts an async grounder** (`src/review/find.ts`). The context grounder is async but `validate` is not, so the finder now collects the grounding answers before validating.\n- **Durations stay in Go nanosecond form** rather than milliseconds, so budget strings like `1m30s` format exactly as Go writes them.\n- **Two `meta.json` fields are approximate.** The scope type from ticket 10 has no base or merge-base OID, so `base_oid` falls back to the snapshot's base and `merge_base_oid` is empty.\n\n**The two-SIGINT test doesn't run the scenario as written.** A fake server that never answers can't produce exit 130, for two reasons:\n- After the first SIGINT, the CLI finishes and exits before Node handles another signal, even one sent 1 ms later.\n- Two identical signals sent back to back merge into one.\n\nThe test therefore uses a fake `git` that takes 300 ms to exit when stopped, and sends the second SIGINT 100 ms after the first. That gives exit 130 with no leftover processes. The one-SIGINT case does run against a server that never answers and exits 5.\n\nThese reasons and other gotchas are in `.redeye/notes.md`; reusable testing notes went into `docs/agents/typescript.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":316,"cache_read_input_tokens":257395,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":316},"output_tokens":783,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b283ca8-677a-43f7-a7e2-25611b063cf7","uuid":"fd0e15ec-a1c9-4a61-8c4e-bf8a65f38ebb","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:48:18.512Z","request_id":"req_011ChLuotDDYC2zfRovWhigo"}
